      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4455407005": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Company\nCareem is building the Everything App for the greater Middle East — making it easy to move around, order food and groceries, manage payments, and more. Our purpose is simple: to simplify and improve people’s lives and build an awesome organisation that inspires.\nSince 2012, Careem has enabled earnings for over 2.5 million Captains, simplified the lives of more than 70 million customers, and built a platform where the region’s best talent and entrepreneurs thrive. We operate in 70+ cities across 10 countries, from Morocco to Pakistan.\nWe’re now entering our next chapter — one powered by AI. We’re looking for AI talent: curious problem-solvers who know how to apply AI to build tools, automate workflows, and create real impact. Whether it’s streamlining operations, enhancing customer experience, or reimagining internal systems — we want people who can make Careem work smarter and move faster.\nAbout the team\nAt Careem, the mission for the NextGen program is to help grow our new joint Engineering by learning how to write Clean Code, use SOLID principle techniques, and design reliable systems. The ultimate goal is to train the new Engineers to build Engineering excellence foundations with high standards. Our program covers all the areas of Careem tech be it Cyber Security, Data, Infrastructure, and all the Software Engineering tracks like Backend, Frontend as well as Mobile.\nWe are looking for software engineers to join our team of talented engineers that share a common interest in distributed backend systems, their scalability, and continued development. You will work alongside a top talent for an accelerated learning path. You will have access to some of the most exciting projects and advanced tech for accelerated learning and exposure.\nYou will be responsible for maintaining some of our services that power the Careem Engine, scaling highly distributed systems, and continuously documenting and improving our engineering practices. These large-scale, distributed systems handle everything from user requests to payment processing.\nWhat you'll do:\nResponsibilities\nOur tech stack is Java 8 and Spring Boot, Micro-Service Architecture, SQL and no-SQL DBs, and AWS infrastructure. Key responsibilities include:\nDevelopment of our distributed backend system to meet the challenging functional, scalability, and reliability requirements for our fast-growing business.\nMaintain features and systems, with an emphasis on code quality, maintainability, readability, and testing.\nFacilitate collaboration with other engineers, product owners, and designers to solve interesting and challenging problems across our platform.\nBe a valued member of an autonomous, cross-functional agile team.\nYou care about quality and you know what it means to ship high-quality code.\nWhat you'll need:\nFresh graduates are encouraged to apply!\nThe ideal candidate will have a passionate commitment to improving the lives of people, an insane focus on excellence and customer service, and a strong alignment with our core values: being bold, focused, agile and collaborative.\nMust have:\nBachelor's Degree in Computer Science or other related technical fields.\nUnderstanding of Object-oriented design, data structures, and algorithms.\nAbility to solve complex problems.\nMust be able to write clean and maintainable code (must love coding!).\nAbility to effectively articulate technical challenges and solutions; deal with loosely defined problems and fast-changing requirements & think abstractly.\nPassionate about learning new technologies and working on a product of massive scale and impact.\nAble to communicate effectively.\nAttention to detail.\nNice to have:\nKnowledge of AWS\nKnowledge of clean code principles\nDeep understanding of design patterns\nDemonstrated ability of test-driven development",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482178713": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Position\nForward Deployed Engineers sit inside the client’s problem, not next to it. You embed with an enterprise team, find the work that actually warrants AI, architect the system, build it, and make it hold up in the real environment.\nThis is a three-way role: consultant, operator, engineer . You should be as comfortable pressure-testing a business case with a COO or VP of Engineering as you are debugging why an agent’s tool-calling loop degraded after a context change. The people who succeed here can hold a discovery conversation on Monday and ship what they scoped on Thursday.\nOn this track, your edge is application engineering: you make agents real inside the client’s actual systems, workflows, and delivery pipelines.\nWe work with regulated industries and Fortune 500 clients who have AI mandates, real constraints, and low tolerance for demos that don’t hold up.\nHow We Approach The Work\nFDEs are trusted to shape the solution, not only deliver it. Every engagement calls for architect-level judgment:\nReframes the request. Treats “we need an agent for X” as a hypothesis, not a spec.\nDecomposes the problem. Outcome → process → decisions → data → systems → actors → constraints — before choosing technology.\nChooses the intervention. Remove, simplify, traditional software, automation, LLM, RAG, agent, or multi-agent — and defends why.\nOwns the architecture decision. Documents trade-offs (ADRs), sets success metrics, pushes back on scope that won’t deliver value.\nConsultative Discovery\nClients rarely arrive with a fully formed problem, and the FDE’s first contribution is helping them see it clearly. You lead discovery with genuine curiosity, moving the conversation from stated requirements to underlying needs, and you build credibility through the depth of your understanding rather than the breadth of your pitch.\nUncovers business drivers. What outcome matters, what it’s worth, why now, and what happens if nothing changes.\nUncovers personal drivers. What each stakeholder is measured on, what they’re worried about, and what a win looks like for them individually.\nSurfaces constraints early. Security, compliance, data access, budget, skills, politics, timelines — the things that kill projects in month two.\nAligns stakeholders. Spots conflicting goals between business, engineering, and risk, and brings them to a shared definition of success.\nAsks strategic questions. Follows the answer with “why,” “how do you know,” and “what happens today when…” — without interrogating. Clients leave the conversation understanding their own problem better.\nEarns authority through depth. Credibility comes from the quality of the questions and the insight in the playback, not from pitching technology.\nWhat You'll Do\nDiscover. Run workshops and process discovery with business and engineering stakeholders. Separate genuine AI problems from workflow problems wearing an AI costume. Come back with a scoped, defensible point of view.\nStructure the process and the spec. For any business or engineering process being automated, map the current state, decision points, and exceptions, then turn it into specifications that both people and AI systems can execute against reliably.\nArchitect & design. Design agentic systems end to end — orchestration, context and retrieval architecture, tool and MCP integration, guardrails, human-in-the-loop checkpoints, and the boundaries between deterministic and non-deterministic components.\nBuild. Ship working systems — agents, multi-step automations, internal tooling, integration layers. You are hands-on. Prototypes that prove value in weeks, not slideware.\nEngineer the delivery system. Own CI/CD for what you build: build, test, release, environments.\nConsult. Present to and defend decisions in front of CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and business leadership. Quantify impact in their terms. Support pre-sales scoping and proposal work when the deal calls for it.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with at least one mainstream production stack (TypeScript/Node.js, Python, Java, C#/.NET, or Go).\n1 - 4 years of professional experience building and shipping LLM-powered and agentic AI systems beyond prototypes or demos.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nHands-on experience with frontier AI developer tools including Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, or OpenAI Codex.\nProven experience evaluating current-state environments and defining technical roadmaps.\nDemonstrated experience with APIs, service design, event-driven and distributed systems, and data modeling.\nExperience designing and owning CI/CD pipelines, including build, test, release, environments, and deployment processes.\nStrong understanding of context and specification engineering to produce reliable AI output.\nSolid understanding of enterprise integration patterns, including APIs, webhooks, event streams, iPaaS platforms such as n8n or MuleSoft, and MCP.\nTrack record of leading client-facing discovery calls, asking \"why\" before \"how\" to decompose unstructured business problems.\nSkilled at exercising end-to-end delivery ownership and managing project scope without requiring product manager supervision.\nAbility to work through new and difficult issues and contribute to libraries as needed.\nAbility to create and maintain continuous integration and delivery of applications.\nForensic attention to detail.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nExperience working on Agile / Scrum teams.\nMeaningful experience working on large, complex systems.\nAbility to take extreme ownership over your work. Every day is a challenge to ensure you are performing to the expectations you and your team have agreed upon.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients, and dedicate yourself to delivering on the commitments you and your team make to them.\nStrong Plus\nProduction AI operations (Day 2): eval harnesses, observability and tracing, cost and token economics, drift, debugging non-deterministic systems.\nPrompt- and eval-level regression testing running in CI and gating releases.\nDelivery in regulated environments (financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing).\nPre-sales support: discovery calls, SOW and estimate shaping, technical proposal defense.\nProcess mining, operations analysis, or transformation consulting background.\nClient enablement and training — building the client team’s capability, not just the system.\nPrior consulting or agency environment; comfort with ambiguity and multiple accounts.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487470092": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We are looking for a Front-End Engineer who is motivated to combine the art of design with the art of programming. Responsibilities will include translation of the UI/UX design wireframes to actual code that will produce visual elements of the application. You will work with the UI/UX designer and bridge the gap between graphical design and technical implementation, taking an active role on both sides and defining how the application looks as well as how it works. Job Responsibilities\nDevelop new user-facing features.\nEnsure the technical feasibility of UI/UX designs.\nOptimize application for maximum speed and scalability.\nWork in multidisciplinary team with other professionals such as back-end developers.\nBuild high-quality mockups and design different prototypes.\nProvide high-quality graphics and visual elements.\nMaintain and improve Solutioninn website.\nSkills Required\nProficient understanding of web markup, including HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap.\nBasic understanding of server-side CSS pre-processing platforms, such as LESS and SASS.\nProficient understanding of client-side scripting and JavaScript frameworks, including jQuery.\nEnable to design responsive and pixel perfect web pages.\nA quick learner who wants to surround himself with a team.\nAn ability to perform well in a fast-paced environment.\nExcellent analytical, multitasking, time-management, interpersonal and communication skills\nGood understanding of advanced JavaScript libraries and frameworks, such as ReactJS, AngularJS is a plus\nBasic knowledge of image authoring tools, to be able to crop, resize, or perform small adjustments on an image. Familiarity with tools such as Photoshop is a plus.\nProficient understanding of cross-browser compatibility issues and ways to work around them.\nProficient understanding of code versioning tools, such as Git.\nGood understanding of SEO principles and ensuring that application will adhere to them.\nRequired Qualifications\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or Software engineering with good CGPA.\nJob Experience\n2 years\nOther Benefits\nBonuses\nCompany Profit Sharing\nFlexible Work Environment\nMedical Coverage\nPetrol Allowance\nLunch Facility\nJob Working Hours 10AM to 7PM Equal Employment Opportunities We provide Equal Employment Opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, disability or genetics. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, compensation, and training.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487819757": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Who We Are:\nAt OPENLANE we make wholesale easy so our customers can be more successful.\nWe’re a technology company building the world’s most advanced—and uncomplicated—digital marketplace for used vehicles.\nWe’re a data company helping customers buy and sell smarter with clear, actionable insights they can understand and use.\nAnd we’re an innovation company accelerating the future of wholesale remarketing through curiosity, collaboration, and an entrepreneurial spirit.\nOur Values:\nDriven Waybuilders . We pursue challenges that inspire us to build, create, and innovate.\nRelentless Curiosity. We seek to understand and improve our customers’ experience.\nSmart Risk-Taking. We transform risk into progress through data, experience, and intuition.\nFearless Ownership. We deliver what we promise and learn along the way.\nWe’re Looking For: We are looking for a motivated and curious Software Engineer to join our engineering team. At OPENLANE, we are a \"Cloud-First, API-First\" organization. In this role, you will work alongside senior engineers to build, maintain, and scale our modern microservices architecture. You will be hands-on with cutting-edge technologies, including AI-assisted development tools and serverless cloud infrastructure, to help solve real-world problems for the automotive finance industry.\nYou Are:\nFirst-Principles Thinking: You love breaking down complex problems into small, manageable parts.\nPassion for Learning: You stay current with new technologies and are eager to master the latest in AI and Cloud.\nCollaborative Spirit: You thrive in a team environment and aren’t afraid to ask questions or seek feedback.\nOwnership: You take pride in the quality of your work and are committed to the success of the team.\nYou Will:\nDevelop & Maintain: Write clean, testable, and efficient code in TypeScript and Node.js.\nExperience in Cloud Architecture: Assist in building and deploying services within a microservices environment on AWS.\nFrontend Contribution: Work with Angular to build intuitive user interfaces for our customers.\nAdopt AI Tools: Leverage modern AI development tools (like GitHub CoPilot or AWS Q) to accelerate your coding and learning.\nCollaborate: Participate in Agile ceremonies (Scrum/Kanban), contribute to code reviews, and work closely with senior mentors to grow your technical skills.\nDatabase Management: Write and optimize SQL queries and work with relational and non-relational databases.\nDevOps Mindset: Utilize CI/CD pipelines (Azure DevOps/GitHub Actions) to ship code frequently and reliably.\nMust Have’s:\nLanguages: Proficiency in TypeScript or JavaScript. Exposure to Object-Oriented languages (Java or C#) is a plus.\nBackend: Foundational knowledge of Node.js and RESTful API design.\n3+ years of hands-on experience in modern front-end frameworks (React, Angular or Vue), including building responsive, user-friendly interfaces\nWorking knowledge of modern JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nTools: Familiarity with Git for version control, and Visual Studio Code.\nEducation: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience).\nNice to Have’s:\nUnderstanding of Clean Code principles and TDD (Test Driven Development).\nFamiliarity with Event-Driven architecture or messaging systems.\nInterest in the FinTech or automotive industry.\nCloud: An interest in AWS (Lambda, S3, DynamoDB).\nWhat We Offer:\nCompetitive pay\nMedical, dental, and vision benefits with employer HSA contributions (US) and FSA options (US)\nImmediately vested 401K (US) or RRSP (Canada) with company match\nPaid Vacation, Personal, and Sick Time\nPaid maternity and paternity leave (US)\nEmployer-paid short-term disability, long-term disability, life insurance, and AD&D (US)\nRobust Employee Assistance Program\nEmployer paid Leap into Service Day to volunteer\nTuition Reimbursement for eligible programs\nOpportunities to expand your skill set and share your knowledge across a publicly traded, global organization\nCompany culture of internal promotions, diverse career paths, and meaningful advancement\nSound like a match? Apply Now - We can't wait to hear from you!\nCompensation Range of\nAnnual Salary: $90,000.00 - $125,000.00\n(Depending on experience, skill set, qualifications, and other relevant factors.)",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487822953": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Req ID: 397029\nNTT DATA strives to hire exceptional, innovative and passionate individuals who want to grow with us. If you want to be part of an inclusive, adaptable, and forward-thinking organization, apply now.\nWe are currently seeking a AWS/Node.js Developer to join our team in McKinney, Texas (US-TX), United States (US).\nWe are seeking a highly skilled and experienced Node.js Developer with deep AWS Cloud expertise to design, build, and maintain our next-generation cloud-native back-end applications. In this role, you will be responsible for developing high-performance RESTful APIs, implementing robust microservices, and managing serverless or containerized architectures within the AWS ecosystem. The ideal candidate is passionate about writing clean, maintainable code, optimizing application performance, and maintaining best-in-class cloud security practices.\nDay to Day/Job Function\nBackend Development: Design, develop, and deploy scalable, secure, and robust server-side applications and microservices using Node.js\nCloud Infrastructure: Build and manage cloud-native solutions using a mix of Serverless architectures (AWS Lambda, API Gateway) and Containerized services\nAPI Integration: Build, optimize, and document secure RESTful APIs and integrate with internal microservices as well as third-party vendors.\nDatabase Management: Design, implement, and maintain efficient database schemas across both SQL (PostgreSQL, MySQL, AWS RDS) and NoSQL (DynamoDB, MongoDB) systems.\nDevOps & CI/CD: Set up and maintain Automated CI/CD pipelines using Git, GitHub Actions, or AWS CodePipeline. Implement Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform or AWS CloudFormation.\nPerformance & Security: Optimize applications for maximum speed, cost efficiency, and scalability. Implement authentication, authorization, and data encryption protocols (IAM, Cognito, OAuth).\nCollaboration & Monitoring: Collaborate closely with frontend developers, DevOps engineers, and product owners in an Agile environment. Troubleshoot production issues and monitor system health using AWS CloudWatch.\nRequired Qualifications:\n5+ years of professional backend development experience focused heavily on Node.js and AWS Cloud Services.\n5+ years of experience in Languages & Frameworks: Strong proficiency in JavaScript (ES6+) and TypeScript, alongside frameworks like Express.js or NestJS.\n5+ years of Core AWS Stack: Hands-on experience with:\nCompute/Serverless: AWS Lambda, EC2, ECS Fargate\nAPI & Integration: API Gateway, SQS, SNS, EventBridge\nStorage & DB: S3, DynamoDB, RDS (PostgreSQL/MySQL)\nSecurity & Operations: IAM, Cognito, Secrets Manager, CloudWatch\nPreferred Qualifications\nTesting: Proficiency in writing comprehensive unit and integration tests using frameworks like Jest or Mocha.\nVersion Control: Mastery of Git workflows.\nEducation:\nBachelor’s or Master's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field (or equivalent professional experience).\nNTT DATA provides a reasonable range of compensation for U.S.-based positions. The starting pay range for this remote role is $102,675.00 to $171,125.00. This range reflects the minimum and maximum target compensation for the position across all US locations.\nActual compensation will depend on a number of factors, including the candidate’s actual work location, relevant experience, technical skills, and other qualifications. This position may also be eligible for incentive compensation based on individual and/or company performance.\nThis position is eligible for company benefits including medical, dental, and vision insurance with an employer contribution, flexible spending or health savings account, life and AD&D insurance, short and long term disability coverage, paid time off, employee assistance, participation in a 401k program with company match, and additional voluntary or legally required benefits\nAbout NTT DATA\nNTT DATA is a $30 billion business and technology services leader, serving 75% of the Fortune Global 100. We are committed to accelerating client success and positively impacting society through responsible innovation. We are one of the world's leading AI and digital infrastructure providers, with unmatched capabilities in enterprise-scale AI, cloud, security, connectivity, data centers and application services. our consulting and Industry solutions help organizations and society move confidently and sustainably into the digital future. As a Global Top Employer, we have experts in more than 50 countries. We also offer clients access to a robust ecosystem of innovation centers as well as established and start-up partners. NTT DATA is a part of NTT Group, which invests over $3 billion each year in R&D.\nWhenever possible, we hire locally to NTT DATA offices or client sites. This ensures we can provide timely and effective support tailored to each client’s needs. While many positions offer remote or hybrid work options, these arrangements are subject to change based on client requirements. For employees near an NTT DATA office or client site, in-office attendance may be required for meetings or events, depending on business needs. At NTT DATA, we are committed to staying flexible and meeting the evolving needs of both our clients and employees. NTT DATA recruiters will never ask for payment or banking information and will only use @nttdata.com, @nttdatafed.com and @talent.nttdataservices.com email addresses. If you are requested to provide payment or disclose banking information, please submit a contact us form, https://us.nttdata.com/en/contact-us.\nNTT DATA endeavors to make https://us.nttdata.com accessible to any and all users. If you would like to contact us regarding the accessibility of our website or need assistance completing the application process, please contact us at https://us.nttdata.com/en/contact-us. This contact information is for accommodation requests only and cannot be used to inquire about the status of applications. NTT DATA is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. For our EEO Policy Statement, please click here. If you'd like more information on your EEO rights under the law, please click here. For Pay Transparency information, please click here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487862669": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Canonical is a leading provider of open source software and operating systems to the global enterprise and technology markets. Our platform, Ubuntu, is very widely used in breakthrough enterprise initiatives such as public cloud, data science, AI, engineering innovation and IoT. Our customers include the world's leading public cloud and silicon providers, and industry leaders in many sectors. The company is a pioneer of global distributed collaboration, with 1200+ colleagues in 75+ countries and very few office-based roles. Teams meet two to four times yearly in person, in interesting locations around the world, to align on strategy and execution.\nThe company is founder-led, profitable, and growing.\nCanonical’s Partner Engineering Team is looking for open-source enthusiasts to work across the full Linux stack to ensure new silicon technologies, such as new hardware accelerators, AI stacks, confidential computing, networking, virtualization, and containerization stacks, are optimized for new silicons.\nPartner Engineering works closely with worldwide silicon companies to optimize Ubuntu for their new silicon, from x86, ARM, RISC-V, PowerPC and s390x architectures.\nLocation: This is a Globally remote role\nThe role entails\nCollaborating proactively within a distributed team\nFostering a software ecosystem with seamless user experience for all Ubuntu users\nEvaluating contributions of other engineers to maintain high-quality software standards.\nPlaying a role in shaping the future of Ubuntu via both - new ideas in your areas of interest and advising on work being done elsewhere\nCollaborating with other teams in the Ubuntu and Debian communities, with upstream projects, and commercially supported customers\nDebugging issues on open source code and team maintained code.\nHelping our our customers to integrate their apps, SDKs, build OS images, optimize applications with Ubuntu Core, Desktop and Server\nWorking with a team to maintain Ubuntu, silicon features, and silicon-optimized packages across platforms and technologies such as:\nServers, HPC and AI systems, IoT devices, PCs, SmartNICs and automotive systems\nAI stacks\nGraphics, audio and multimedia stacks\nVirtualisation and Containers\nHardware enablement stacks\nNew architectures, architecture variants and optimized toolchains\nPackage management and dependencies\nPlatform security (secure boot, FDE, Ubuntu Core, Confidential Computing)\nWork from home with global travel 2 to 4 weeks for internal events\nWhat we are looking for in you\nExceptional academic track record from both high school and university\nUndergraduate degree in a technical subject or a compelling narrative about your alternative chosen path\nYou love technology and working with brilliant people\nYou are curious, flexible, articulate, and accountable\nYou value soft skills and are passionate, enterprising, thoughtful, and self-motivated\nYou value building partnerships with a diverse set of internal and external groups\nStrong fundamentals in C, C++ and Python\nExperience or interest in learning Linux distribution packaging\nExperience or Interest in open source maintenance or contribution and licenses\nFundamental understanding of package management and dependency resolution\nAdditional Skills That You Might Also Bring\nExperience with one or more of the following:\nGraphics, audio, or multimedia stacks\nVirtualization and containers (Docker, OCI, Kubernetes)\nHardware enablement for platforms and devices, including SmartNICs, NVMe storage, GPUs, audio components, and sensors\nPerformance optimization\nToolchain development and maintenance\nNetworking protocols and technologies (TCP/IP, DHCP, HTTP/REST)\nSecurity best practices\nIoT and embedded systems, including board-level hardware, SoCs, BMCs, bootloaders, firmware, operating systems, applications, and services\nWhat we offer colleagues\nWe consider geographical location, experience, and performance in shaping compensation worldwide. We revisit compensation annually (and more often for graduates and associates) to ensure we recognize outstanding performance. In addition to base pay, we offer a performance-driven annual bonus or commission. We provide all team members with additional benefits which reflect our values and ideals. We balance our programs to meet local needs and ensure fairness globally.\nDistributed work environment with twice-yearly team sprints in person\nPersonal learning and development budget of USD 2,000 per year\nAnnual compensation review\nRecognition rewards\nAnnual holiday leave\nMaternity and paternity leave\nTeam Member Assistance Program & Wellness Platform\nOpportunity to travel to new locations to meet colleagues\nPriority Pass and travel upgrades for long-haul company events\nAbout Canonical\nCanonical is a pioneering tech firm that is at the forefront of the global move to open source. As the company that publishes Ubuntu, one of the most important open source projects and the platform for AI, IoT and the cloud, we are changing the world on a daily basis. We recruit on a global basis and set a very high standard for people joining the company. We expect excellence - in order to succeed, we need to be the best at what we do. Canonical has been a remote-first company since its inception in 2004. Working here is a step into the future, and will challenge you to think differently, work smarter, learn new skills, and raise your game.\nCanonical is an equal opportunity employer\nWe are proud to foster a workplace free from discrimination. Diversity of experience, perspectives, and background create a better work environment and better products. Whatever your identity, we will give your application fair consideration.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487877138": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Intelligems builds the AI agents that turn your traffic into profit. Every day, brands makes thousands of decisions — what to show, what to offer, how to price for each visitor — and most of them happen by default. We build the data and the agents that make those decisions for you, automatically, so your site gets smarter with every visitor instead of sitting static. Our mission is to make every one of those decisions intelligent: grounded in what actually works, not guesswork.\nWe have excellent traction: we’re working with over 3,000 brands and have access to more than $10B of transaction and shopping session data. We are looking for highly talented individuals to join us and help us continue to scale efficiently. We have an extremely high-performing team, with a collaborative culture of low-ego + high-IQ people. Our people are our strongest asset, and we hold a very high bar.\nWe're backed by Stage 2 Ventures, Vinyl Capital, Matchstick Ventures, Techstars, and the founders of companies like Klaviyo and Postscript, and have raised >$11M to date.\nThe Role\nRoll up your sleeves and let’s build together! From day one, we’ll ask you to contribute to any and every aspect of our stack. It could be adding new functionality to the core experimentation capabilities of the platform, designing and implementing a new integration, or reworking a complicated user flow.\nOur team is lean and mean — less than 20 engineers and only a handful of product and design. This means you’ll work closely with everyone, including those in non-technical roles like our sales, support, and success teams.\nMonth one will be characterized by “learning by doing” - taking on features that are meaningful in impact with input from other teammates to get deep in the codebase and concepts while also providing value to our customers.\nFrom there you’ll tackle increasingly complex and ambiguous problems. With varying degrees of input from your product and design teammates, you’ll figure out the implementation details from schema and API design to UI polish.\nWe have thousands of customers, too, so there are often opportunities to work directly or indirectly with them. Understanding the customer perspective and having empathy are important skills that will help make you effective in each of the countless micro design decisions you make each day.\nTech Stack\nKnowledge in all of these is not required, but you should be excited to work within and help us improve the stack.\nTypeScript monorepo\nFrontend - React web app hosted on AWS S3/Cloudfront; Redux, Material UI, ReactQuery\nBackend - Serverless NodeJS hosted on AWS Lambda, managed by SST. MySQL database. Also includes SQS queues, Dynamo tables, dockerized lambdas, etc….\n“Plugin” - Compiled client-side javascript written in Typescript\nAnalytics - AWS Eventbus, Kinesis, Flink, Kafka, and Clickhouse.\nYou’re a Great Fit If\nYou have experience owning product and feature development from ideation to delivery\nYou’re able to hold a lot of context in your head — there are a lot of moving pieces here to keep in mind\nExploration, learning, and experimentation are core to your process\nYou have deep expertise in areas that will level us up\nAt the same time have curiosity to learn try a different approach\nYou empathize with our customers, and care deeply about making them successful\nYou're a team player and can work collaboratively while also being independent\nYou want to shape the future of e-commerce\nNote: please only apply to ONE software engineering role at Intelligems. We are able to move candidates between the Frontend & Full Stack roles as needed.\nBenefits for full-time employees:\nCompetitive salary and equity packages\nMedical, dental, and vision insurance (varies by country)\n401k + match (U.S. only)\nFlexible PTO policy\nParental leave\n$ to spend quarterly with our growing list of brands\nWFH setup stipend\nLaptop provided\nTeam meetups and events\nBenefits & perks may vary outside of the U.S.\nIntelligems is a remote-first company with 4 offices (NYC, Denver, Boston, and Chicago), but please note that some travel may be required.\nAll Intelligems interviews are transcribed by an AI notetaker.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487894751": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates within the healthcare sector, addressing the challenges of improving patient care and healthcare delivery through a collaborative and integrated team approach. With a presence across 900 practices nationwide serving over 14.5 million patients annually, the organization focuses on transforming healthcare from within by fostering a culture centered on collective achievements and community impact.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER I role involves full lifecycle software application development to support the organization's healthcare initiatives. This position contributes by developing, testing, and deploying software solutions, participating in Agile processes, and supporting production environments. The role also engages in research and development activities related to generative AI, enhancing the organization's technological capabilities and operational efficiency.\nResponsibilities:\nParticipate in software application and business logic development.\nEngage in Agile/Scrum sessions and project planning.\nConduct code reviews, write code and tests.\nContribute to generative AI research and development.\nAssist with deployment, testing, and validation on QA environments.\nSupport production deployment, validation, troubleshooting, and support.\nMonitor applications and automate processes.\nRequirements:\nBachelor’s degree in information technology or related field.\nPreferably one year of software development experience.\nFamiliarity with generative AI technology preferred.\nExperience with Microsoft Azure platform tools preferred.\nKnowledge of programming languages such as C#, Java, or Python.\nUnderstanding of databases, operating systems, and MS SQL.\nExperience with RESTful APIs, database programming, and UI programming.\nAbility to write maintainable code in C# and SQL.\nWillingness to learn new technologies quickly.\nExposure to CSS, Powershell, JavaScript.\nBasic knowledge of machine learning and generative AI concepts.\nExperience with version control systems like GitHub and familiarity with CI/CD.\nUnderstanding of Agile methodologies is a plus.\nAbility to work collaboratively and communicate effectively in English.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nBase salary range is $69,520 to $86,900, excluding fringe benefits and potential bonuses.\nEligibility to participate in an annual corporate success sharing bonus based on organizational performance.\nFinal compensation depends on skills, education, and experience.\nBenefits & Perks:\nSuperior health plan options\nDental and vision insurance\nHealth savings and flexible spending accounts\nLife and accidental death and dismemberment coverage\n401(k) retirement savings plan with matching and profit-sharing contributions\nGenerous paid time off starting at 3 to 4 weeks annually\nStudent loan refinancing discounts\nProfessional and career development programs\nEmployee assistance program and travel assistance\nWellness programs\nFlexible work hours\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487899528": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Location: Karachi, Pakistan\nType: Full-Time | Hybrid (Transitioning to On-Site)\nSalary: PKR 90,000–120,000/month\nExperience: 2 - 4 Years\nWe're looking for a skilled Flutter Engineer who understands not just how to write code, but how to build scalable, performant, and beautifully designed mobile applications.\nKey Requirements:\n- Strong proficiency in Flutter and Dart.\n- Excellent UI/UX understanding with the ability to translate Figma designs into pixel-perfect, responsive applications.\n- Solid understanding of Flutter's widget lifecycle, rendering, and performance optimization.\n- Experience with state management (Riverpod, BLoC, Provider, etc.).\n- Familiarity with Clean Architecture, SOLID principles, and maintainable code.\n- Understanding of mobile application security, authentication, and secure data handling.\n- Experience with REST APIs, third-party integrations, and Git.\n- Strong debugging, analytical thinking, and problem-solving skills.\n- Have experience in compliance with Google and Apple app stores' policies\nWhat We Value:\nWe're looking for someone who thinks critically, takes ownership, and focuses on solving problems rather than just completing tasks.\nExperience developing and deploying production-ready Android and iOS applications is highly preferred.\nSend your CV along with your portfolio, GitHub profile, or links to published applications via LinkedIn DM.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488647268": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Multi Media, LLC\nMulti Media, LLC is a global technology company operating a high-traffic live-streaming platform used by millions of people around the world. Behind the experience is a team solving challenging problems in real-time video, scalability, reliability, data, machine learning, and user experience.\nWe’re a place for people who want their work to matter. Our teams have the autonomy to make decisions, the opportunity to work on problems at meaningful scale, and the ability to see their work shape experiences for a global audience in real time. We value curiosity, ownership, collaboration, and continuous improvement.\nThe Role\nWe are looking for a frontend-leaning Software Engineer to join our Viewer team and help build user-facing features that reach millions of people worldwide.\nYou'll primarily work with React and JavaScript/TypeScript, collaborating closely with product, design, QA, and other engineers to deliver meaningful improvements to the user experience. We're looking for someone who enjoys solving problems beyond writing code, understands the value of the features they're building, and is excited to leverage modern development tools, including AI, to work more effectively.\nThis is a great opportunity for an early-career engineer who is eager to grow their technical skills, take ownership of their work, and contribute to the broader product development process.\nWhat You’ll Do\nDesign, develop, and maintain user-facing features using React, JavaScript/TypeScript, and Python\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code\nCollaborate with engineers, product managers, designers, and QA to build and improve features\nParticipate in code reviews, debugging, and troubleshooting\nContribute to technical discussions and help identify solutions to engineering challenges\nWork with experienced engineers to learn best practices and grow your technical skills\nTake ownership of assigned tasks and see features through development, testing, and deployment\nHelp improve the performance, reliability, and overall user experience of our platform\nRequirements\nYou Have\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field (or equivalent practical experience)\nFoundational experience in web development\nExperience writing production code in JavaScript/TypeScript and/or Python\nExperience working with React in a professional or substantial project setting\nFamiliarity with backend frameworks such as Django, Flask, or similar\nStrong debugging, problem-solving, and critical thinking skills\nAbility to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams, including product, design, and QA\nOwnership mindset and ability to manage tasks through completion with guidance\nInterest in understanding user needs and the impact of your work on the product\nCuriosity and willingness to learn new technologies, including AI-assisted development tools\nCollaborative, adaptable, and open to feedback\nBonus Points\nExperience shipping full-stack features end-to-end\nHands-on experience using AI coding assistants to improve development workflows\nExperience working with QA teams, writing tests, or improving software quality\nExperience with AWS or GCP\nExperience working on high-traffic applications\nBenefits\nWhat You’ll Get\nFair and competitive base salary\nFully Remote Optional\nHealth, Vision, Dental, and Life Insurances for you and any dependents, with policy premiums covered by the Company\nLong & Short term disability insurance\nUnlimited PTO\nAnnual Year-End Company Closure\nOptional 401k with 5% matching\n12 Paid Holidays\nPaid Lunches in-office, or if Remote, a $125/week stipend via Sharebite\nEAP and Employee Recognition Programs\nAnd much more!\nThe base salary range for this position is $130,000 - $165,000 annually, plus additional compensation and benefits. The range displayed reflects the minimum and maximum range for a new hire across the U.S. for the posted position. A candidate's specific pay will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the candidate's job-related skills, relevant education, training, experience, certifications, and abilities, as well as other factors unique to each candidate.\nMulti Media, LLC, is an equal opportunity employer that values diversity. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488749360": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Optum Tech is a global leader in health care innovation. Our teams develop cutting-edge solutions that help people live healthier lives and help make the health system work better for everyone. From advanced data analytics and AI to cybersecurity, we use innovative approaches to solve some of health care's most complex challenges. Your contributions here have the potential to change lives. Ready to build the next breakthrough? Join us to start Caring. Connecting. Growing together.\nSoftware engineering is the application of engineering to the design, development, implementation, testing and maintenance of software in a systematic method. The roles in this function will cover all primary development activity across all technology functions that ensure we deliver code with high quality for our applications, products and services and to understand customer needs and to develop product roadmaps.\nThese roles include, but are not limited to analysis, design, coding, engineering, testing, debugging, standards, methods, tools analysis, documentation, research and development, maintenance, new development, operations and delivery. With every role in the company, each position has a requirement for building quality into every output. This also includes evaluating new tools, new techniques, strategies; Automation of common tasks; build of common utilities to drive organizational efficiency with a passion around technology and solutions and influence of thought and leadership on future capabilities and opportunities to apply technology in new and innovative ways.\nYou'll enjoy the flexibility to work remotely * from anywhere within the U.S. as you take on some tough challenges. For all hires in the Minneapolis or Washington, D.C. area, you will be required to work in the office a minimum of four days per week.\nPrimary Responsibilities\nImplement end-to-end features and user stories, including analysis, design, development, validation, deployment, and post-deployment support\nAnalyze and document business logic in existing and legacy applications, and re-implement it as maintainable, well-tested software\nDesign, build, and optimize computation-intensive processing - improving the runtime, scalability, and accuracy of calculation-heavy workloads\nBuild and maintain validation and parity-testing frameworks that verify new implementations produce results consistent with the systems they replace\nWork with relational databases and modern data platforms to design, query, and optimize data models and pipelines\nApply security principles and industry best practices when designing and building secure applications and APIs, including safeguarding sensitive and confidential data\nContribute to the design and adoption of architectural patterns, engineering standards, and reusable frameworks\nBuild, maintain, and improve CI/CD pipelines, code quality gates, and test automation frameworks\nTroubleshoot, diagnose, and resolve issues across development, test, and production environments, including correctness and precision defects in calculation logic\nCollaborate within Agile development teams, and directly with business and analytical subject matter experts, to translate domain rules into technical requirements and validated solutions\nLeverage AI tools (including Copilot and related AI Builder tools) to enhance development productivity and efficiency\nDemonstrate solid problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and effective collaboration across teams\nYou'll be rewarded and recognized for your performance in an environment that will challenge you and give you clear direction on what it takes to succeed in your role as well as provide development for other roles you may be interested in.\nRequired Qualifications\n4+ years of hands-on software development experience using Python, with exposure to modern front-end frameworks such as React.js\n4+ years of experience working on modern software engineering technologies, with a solid focus on API development (RESTful services using FastAPI, Flask, Django, or similar)\n3+ years of experience developing data-intensive or analytical applications using pandas, NumPy, or comparable libraries\n3+ years of experience working with relational databases, including data modelling, complex queries, and query optimization\n3+ years of experience working in Agile/Scrum development environments\n3+ years of experience in cloud-native development using platforms such as Azure, or GCP, and working with containerization (Docker) and orchestration tools (Kubernetes)\n1+ years of experience in applying numerical or algorithmic methods - iterative solvers, root-finding, optimization, or convergence and precision analysis\n1+ years of experience in developing secure RESTful APIs and service-oriented architectures\n1+ years of experience in CI/CD pipelines and automated testing practices\n1+ years of experience in ability to effectively use AI-powered development tools (e.g., Copilot) to improve productivity\nPreferred Qualifications\nBachelor's degree in Engineering, Information Technology, Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics, or a related field\nExperience modernizing legacy or end-user-computing applications (spreadsheet- or macro-based business logic) into production software\nExperience with distributed or parallel computing frameworks (Spark, Dask, Ray, or equivalent)\nExperience with Databricks or a comparable lakehouse/data platform, including medallion (bronze/silver/gold) architecture\nExperience with data governance, lineage, quality, and access-control frameworks\nExperience with monitoring and observability tools such as Dynatrace, Splunk, Grafana, or similar platforms\nHealthcare payer, actuarial, pricing, or financial-modelling domain experience\nAll employees working remotely will be required to adhere to UnitedHealth Group's Telecommuter Policy.\nPay is based on several factors including but not limited to local labor markets, education, work experience, certifications, etc. In addition to your salary, we offer benefits such as, a comprehensive benefits package, incentive and recognition programs, equity stock purchase and 401k contribution (all benefits are subject to eligibility requirements). No matter where or when you begin a career with us, you'll find a far-reaching choice of benefits and incentives. The salary for this role will range from $72,800 - $130,000 annually based on full-time employment. We comply with all minimum wage laws as applicable.\nApplication Deadline: This will be posted for a minimum of 2 business days or until a sufficient candidate pool has been collected. Job posting may come down early due to volume of applicants.\nAt UnitedHealth Group, our mission is to help people live healthier lives and make the health system work better for everyone. We believe everyone-of every race, gender, sexuality, age, location and income-deserves the opportunity to live their healthiest life. Today, however, there are still far too many barriers to good health which are disproportionately experienced by people of color, historically marginalized groups and those with lower incomes. We are committed to mitigating our impact on the environment and enabling and delivering equitable care that addresses health disparities and improves health outcomes - an enterprise priority reflected in our mission.\nUnitedHealth Group is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer under applicable law and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, national origin, religion, age, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by local, state, or federal laws, rules, or regulations.\nUnitedHealth Group is a drug - free workplace. Candidates are required to pass a drug test before beginning employment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488936551": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Overview\nFounded in Dubai in 2016, SQUATWOLF is a gym wear brand made for athletes who push limits, in and out of the gym. What started in the Middle East has grown into a global movement, with customers in 100+ countries. We’re on a mission to elevate the human experience through high-performance gear that drives strength, progress, and purpose.\nYour Role\nWe are looking for a motivated Mobile Application Engineer (React Native) with 1–3 years of experience to join our engineering team. The ideal candidate should have hands-on experience building, maintaining, and improving cross-platform mobile applications for Android and iOS.\nYou will work closely with senior engineers, designers, and backend developers to develop reliable, high-performance mobile applications and deliver an excellent user experience.\nWhat you will do\nDevelop and maintain cross-platform mobile applications using React Native.\nBuild reusable, scalable, and maintainable components using JavaScript or TypeScript.\nIntegrate RESTAPIs and handle asynchronous data, loading states, and error scenarios.\nImplement state management using tools such as Redux Toolkit or React Context.\nCollaborate with UI/UX designers to translate designs into responsive, pixel-perfect interfaces.\nDebug issues, fix bugs, and optimize application performance.\nWork with native Android and iOS configurations when required.\nIntegrate third-party libraries and SDKs, such as Firebase, push notifications, and analytics tools.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow coding standards and best practices.\nAssist with application testing, release builds, and publishing updates to the Google Play Store and Apple App Store.\nWork with Git and participate in Agile development processes.\nWhat we are looking for\n1–3 years of hands-on experience in React Native development.\nGood understanding of JavaScript (ES6+) and TypeScript fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with React concepts, including hooks, functional components, props, and state.\nExperience integrating REST APIs and handling JSON responses.\nUnderstanding of state management solutions such as Redux Toolkit or Context API.\nFamiliarity with navigation libraries, such as React Navigation.\nUnderstanding of mobile application layouts, responsive design, and platform-specific behavior.\nBasic knowledge of Git, debugging, and troubleshooting.\nFamiliarity with Android and iOS development environments.\nGood problem-solving skills and willingness to learn new technologies.\nAbility to work collaboratively in a team environment.\nHands-on experience using AI coding tools such as Cursor and Claude.\nNice to have\nExperience publishing applications to the Google Play Store or Apple App Store.\nFamiliarity withFirebase Analytics, Crashlytics, and push notifications.\nExperience with performance optimisation, caching, and memorymanagement.\nBasic understanding of native Android (Kotlin/Java) or iOS (Swift/Objective-C).\nExperience writing unit tests or component tests.\nWhy SQUATWOLF\nWe reward energy, ownership, and people who take initiative.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488948133": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Overview\nFounded in Dubai in 2016, SQUATWOLF is a gym wear brand made for athletes who push limits, in and out of the gym. What started in the Middle East has grown into a global movement, with customers in 100+ countries. We’re on a mission to elevate the human experience through high-performance gear that drives strength, progress, and purpose.\nYour Role\nWe are looking for a Frontend Engineer (React/ Next.js) with 1–3 years of experience to join our engineering team and help maintain and grow SQUATWOLF’s headless e-commerce store front. You will work closely with a senior engineer, designers, product and backend developers. You will ship UI features, fix bugs, keep the site fast and SEO-friendly, and look after the marketing and analytics integrations the business relies on.\nWhat you will do\nDevelop and maintain a production e-commerce storefront using React and Next.js.\nBuild reusable, maintainable components in TypeScript, styled with Tailwind CSS.\nWork with Server Components, Client Components, layouts, route handlers and Server Actions.\nChoose the right rendering and caching approach (SSR, static, ISR / revalidation, or client-side) foreach page, based on performance and SEO needs.\nIntegrate the Shopify Storefront Graph QL API (products, collections, cart) and our in-house REST API. Handle loading states, caching and errors.\nBuild and maintain a multi-store, multilingual storefront: English and Arabic (RTL), several countries and currencies, and locale-aware routing.\nTurn Figmadesigns into responsive, accessible interfaces that work in both LTR and RTL.\nImprove Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) through image optimization, code splitting and lazy loading.\nIntegrate and maintain third-party services: tag managers and analytics (GTM, Meta, TikTok, Snapchat, Klaviyo and others), search and recommendations, reviews, loyalty, customer support chat and cross-border commerce.\nDebug issues and ensure the site works across browsers and devices, including the mobile app web view.\nVerify changes for each regional store before release and support QA and product sign-off.\nWhat we are looking for\n1–3 years of hands-on React experience, with practical Next.js experience (App Router preferred).\nGood understanding of JavaScript (ES6+) and TypeScript.\nStrong grasp of React fundamentals: hooks, functional components, props, state and component lifecycle.\nUnderstanding of Next.js routing, data fetching, Server Components vs Client Components, and rendering strategies (SSR, SSG, ISR).\nExperience consuming Graph QL APIs, as well as REST APIs and JSON responses.\nProficiency in HTML5, CSS3and responsive design, with hands-on Tailwind CSS experience.\nExperience with, or a strong interest in, internationalization (i18n), including right-to-left (Arabic) layouts.\nUnderstanding of state management with React Context or similar.\nBasic understanding of web performance and SEO principles.\nComfortable with Git, browser Dev Tools, debugging and troubleshooting.\nCareful, detail-oriented approach to changes on a live, revenue-generating site.\nGood problem-solving skills, willingness to learn, and the ability to work well in a team.\nHands-on experience using AI coding tools such as Cursorand Claude.\nNice to Have\nExperience with the Shopify Storefront API, Shopify customer accounts, or other headless commerce platforms.\nExperience with multi-region or multi-currency e-commerce.\nFamiliarity with analytics and tracking tools (Google Tag Manager, GA4, Meta Pixel / Conversions API, Klaviyo).\nExperience writing unit, component or end-to-end tests (Jest, React Testing Library, Playwright).\nWhy SQUATWOLF\nWe reward energy, ownership, and people who take initiative.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489003621": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description\nDarkthorn Labs specializes in designing cutting-edge, efficient software solutions that drive business productivity and enhance customer experiences. We are committed to innovation and quality, helping businesses transform processes and achieve their goals. By leveraging technology, we create tools that have a meaningful impact, empowering organizations to excel in competitive markets.\nRole Description\nThis is a full-time on-site role for a Node.js / React Developer located in Lahore. The role involves designing and developing scalable applications using Node.js and React, building and optimizing both front-end and back-end components, and collaborating with team members to deliver high-quality software solutions. Responsibilities also include maintaining code quality, troubleshooting, and ensuring seamless integration of components.\nQualifications\n- Minimum 3 years of professional experience in either Node.js or React (or both)\n- Proficiency in Front-End Development with React\n- Strong Back-End Web Development skills, particularly in Node.js\n- Expertise in Software Development and JavaScript fundamentals\n- Experience with TypeScript and its practical applications\n- Hands-on experience using AI coding agents such as Claude Code, Cursor, or similar\n- Working knowledge of both SQL and NoSQL databases\n- Experience with Linux systems and AWS (particularly EC2)\n- Ability to write clean, maintainable, and efficient code\n- Strong problem-solving and debugging skills\n- Excellent teamwork and collaboration abilities\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489646933": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Responsibilities\nKforce's client in Lakewood, CO is seeking a Golang/Python Developer responsible for supporting existing software products while building a new greenfield application. Summary: This role offers the opportunity to work across the full software development lifecycle, including requirements gathering, solution design, technical specifications, application development, database work, front-end development, and DevOps. The ideal candidate is a well-rounded software engineer who enjoys working across the full stack rather than focusing exclusively on one component of an application. The role is weighted toward backend development, but hands-on front-end experience is required. What You'll Do:\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain software applications across the full stack\nDevelop backend applications using Go and Python\nBuild and maintain front-end applications using React, JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, and CSS\nWork with relational databases, including PostgreSQL\nSupport two existing software products while contributing to the development of a new greenfield product that will consolidate capabilities from those applications\nParticipate throughout the development lifecycle, from gathering requirements and designing solutions through coding and deployment\nContribute to DevOps responsibilities\nHelp evaluate technical approaches and influence technology decisions for a product still being defined\nParticipate actively in stand-ups, ask questions, challenge assumptions constructively, and contribute ideas to improve the product and engineering approach\nExperiment with different solutions and work in an agile environment that emphasizes iteration and learning quickly\nRequirements\n3-5 years of professional software engineering experience\nExperience developing software applications using Go and Python, or a strong software engineering background with transferable experience in comparable languages\nFull-stack development experience with a strong backend foundation\nExperience working with SQL databases such as PostgreSQL\nAbility to understand and contribute across multiple layers of an application rather than working exclusively within a single area such as APIs or databases\nAbility to explain technical decisions, coding approaches, and problem-solving methodology\nStrong communication skills and willingness to contribute actively within a small engineering team\nExperience developing front-end web applications using:\nReact\nJavaScript\nTypeScript\nHTML\nCSS\nExperience in any of the following would be highly valuable:\nTimescaleDB or other time-series databases\nEvent-driven systems\nInternet of Things (IoT) applications\nAI-enabled development environments\nGreenfield product development\nDevOps\nDatabase schema design\nEnd-to-end product development\nUI/UX principles or the ability to provide thoughtful input on front-end design and usability\nThis role is best suited for an engineer who wants broad ownership rather than a narrowly defined development function. The team is specifically looking for someone who will speak up during stand-ups, ask questions, constructively challenge assumptions, and bring a forward-thinking, entrepreneurial approach to engineering.\nThe pay range is the lowest to highest compensation we reasonably in good faith believe we would pay at posting for this role. We may ultimately pay more or less than this range. Employee pay is based on factors like relevant education, qualifications, certifications, experience, skills, seniority, location, performance, union contract and business needs. This range may be modified in the future.\nWe offer comprehensive benefits including medical/dental/vision insurance, HSA, FSA, 401(k), and life, disability & ADD insurance to eligible employees. Salaried personnel receive paid time off. Hourly employees are not eligible for paid time off unless required by law. Hourly employees on a Service Contract Act project are eligible for paid sick leave.\nNote: Pay is not considered compensation until it is earned, vested and determinable. The amount and availability of any compensation remains in Kforce's sole discretion unless and until paid and may be modified in its discretion consistent with the law.\nThis job is not eligible for bonuses, incentives or commissions.\nKforce is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, or disability status.\nBy clicking “Apply Today” you agree to receive calls, AI-generated calls, text messages or emails from Kforce and its affiliates, and service providers. Note that if you choose to communicate with Kforce via text messaging the frequency may vary, and message and data rates may apply. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. You will always have the right to cease communicating via text by using key words such as STOP.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489656369": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "What You Can Expect\nAs a Software Engineer on our platform team, you will own and deliver full features independently, building reliable APIs and data infrastructure that directly shape the customer experience. Your technical instincts for scalability, observability, and performance will help keep our systems ahead of product demand, giving the broader engineering organization a strong foundation to build on. You will collaborate with experienced application and front-end engineers, using customer problems as your primary input for designing clean, maintainable solutions. Candidates who do not have meaningful backend engineering experience or are uncomfortable working at the intersection of systems design and product development are unlikely to be a strong fit for this role.\nAbout The Team\nOur engineering team builds the data infrastructure and intelligence systems that power Zoom’s go-to-market platform, bringing together signals, data orchestration, and execution workflows in one unified environment. We operate at the intersection of scale and complexity, supporting organizations that depend on reliable, real-time data to move faster and smarter. Our work directly influences how Zoom’s GTM teams and customers drive outcomes, making our systems among the most strategically important in the company.\nResponsibilities\nDesign and build infrastructure, data models, and APIs that power core platform features and resolve real customer problems at scale.\nShip well-designed, testable code with a consistent focus on performance, scalability, and long-term reliability.\nBuild and maintain software testing, validation procedures, and technical documentation that uphold engineering quality standards.\nOwn core internal infrastructure and ML systems, ensuring they reliably serve the evolving needs of customers and cross-functional teams.\nAnalyze complex system challenges and deliver simple, elegant solutions that account for observability, SLA commitments, and long-term scalability.\nWhat We’re Looking For\n6+ years of experience in software engineering, with a strong focus on backend systems and API development.\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent experience.\nSolid hands-on experience with AWS, Postgres, and Node.js, including production-level deployment and operations.\nProficiency across the application stack: TypeGraphQL, Apollo/Express, React, RDS, and ClickHouse.\nDemonstrated ownership of large-scale backend projects, with genuine pride in craft and code quality.\nClear and effective communication with cross-functional engineering teams, including application and front-end engineers.\nSound judgment on technical tradeoffs, a preference for stable and well-supported solutions, and a knack for turning customer problems into simple, scalable system designs.\nSalary Range Or On Target Earnings\n$98,900.00 - $228,700.00\nIn addition to the base salary and/or OTE listed Zoom has a Total Direct Compensation philosophy that takes into consideration; base salary, bonus and equity value.\nNote: Starting pay will be based on a number of factors and commensurate with qualifications & experience.\nWe also have a location based compensation structure; there may be a different range for candidates in this and other locations\nAt Zoom, we offer a window of at least 5 days for you to apply because we believe in giving you every opportunity. Below is the potential closing date, just in case you want to mark it on your calendar. We look forward to receiving your application!\nAnticipated Position Close Date\n11/20/26\nWays of Working\nOur structured hybrid approach is centered around our offices and remote work environments. The work style of each role, Hybrid, Remote, or In-Person is indicated in the job description/posting.\nBenefits\nAs part of our award-winning workplace culture and commitment to delivering happiness, our benefits program offers a variety of perks, benefits, and options to help employees maintain their physical, mental, emotional, and financial health; support work-life balance; and contribute to their community in meaningful ways. Click Learn for more information.\nAbout Us\nZoomies help people stay connected so they can get more done together. We set out to build the best collaboration platform for the enterprise, and today help people communicate better with products like Zoom Contact Center, Zoom Phone, Zoom Events, Zoom Apps, Zoom Rooms, and Zoom Webinars.\nWe’re problem-solvers, working at a fast pace to design solutions with our customers and users in mind. Find room to grow with opportunities to stretch your skills and advance your career in a collaborative, growth-focused environment.\nOur Commitment\nAt Zoom, we believe great work happens when people feel supported and empowered. We’re committed to fair hiring practices that ensure every candidate is evaluated based on skills, experience, and potential. If you require an accommodation during the hiring process, let us know—we’re here to support you at every step.\nIf you need assistance navigating the interview process due to a medical disability, please submit an Accommodations Request Form and someone from our team will reach out soon. This form is solely for applicants who require an accommodation due to a qualifying medical disability. Non-accommodation-related requests, such as application follow-ups or technical issues, will not be addressed.\nOur interviews are supported by BrightHire, a tool that helps us create a consistent and thoughtful interview experience and may include recordings. Please refer to our candidate privacy statement for more information of how we use your data.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489664390": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Unrivaled\nUnrivaled is a premier professional women’s 3v3 basketball league showcasing the top players in the sport. Our mission is to elevate the profile of women’s basketball through exceptional talent, groundbreaking partnerships, and unparalleled fan experiences.\nJob Overview\nWe're a collaborative, product-focused engineering team building the technology platform behind one of the fastest-growing leagues in professional sports. We're looking for a Software Engineer who embraces AI-native software development and is excited to use emerging technologies to build better products, solve problems, and accelerate development.\nWe value demonstrated technical ability, creativity, and execution over traditional measures of experience. The ideal candidate combines a strong foundation in software engineering with the ability to leverage AI throughout the development process, while exercising sound technical judgment and maintaining high standards for code quality.\nYou'll work alongside experienced engineers, contributing across our web platform, mobile app, and internal systems while gaining full-stack experience.\nIf you're curious, resourceful, and excited about how AI is transforming software development, we'd love to hear from you.\nKey Responsibilities\nBuild and enhance fan-facing product experiences, including player profiles, game statistics, live scoring, fan voting, challenges, newsletters, and other interactive features.\nDevelop internal tools that support league operations, content management, player administration, media workflows, data analysis and reporting, and game operations.\nLeverage AI throughout the software development lifecycle to accelerate development, improve productivity, solve technical problems, and enhance code quality.\nContribute to full-stack product development, including user interfaces, server-side functionality, database interactions, validation, and application security.\nMaintain and improve integrations with third-party platforms and internal services.\nHelp build and enhance our Expo/React Native mobile application.\nTroubleshoot bugs, improve application performance, and contribute to ongoing platform stability.\nEvaluate, test, and refine AI-generated code to ensure accuracy, security, reliability, and maintainability.\nParticipate in code reviews and collaborate with teammates to maintain high-quality, maintainable code.\nWork closely with Product, Design, and other stakeholders to deliver features that improve the fan and employee experience.\nStay current with emerging AI capabilities and identify opportunities to improve engineering workflows and product development.\nQualifications\nDemonstrated proficiency in AI-assisted software development, including the ability to effectively use AI to write, test, debug, and improve code.\nStrong foundation in software engineering principles, with the ability to independently evaluate and refine AI-generated solutions.\nDemonstrated ability to build functional applications or software products, whether through professional experience, independent projects, or other practical work.\nStrong foundation in JavaScript or TypeScript.\nExperience building applications with React.\nWorking knowledge of HTML, CSS, and responsive web development.\nExperience working with Git, pull requests, and collaborative software development workflows.\nExperience integrating APIs and debugging applications.\nAbility to understand and extend an existing codebase while following established engineering patterns.\nStrong problem-solving skills, technical judgment, and attention to detail.\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\nDemonstrated curiosity, ownership, adaptability, and a commitment to continuous learning.\nAbility to thrive in a collaborative, fast-paced product environment.\nBonus Qualifications\nExperience with Next.js or React Native/Expo.\nExperience with relational databases such as PostgreSQL.\nExperience with modern ORMs and API development.\nExperience building AI-powered features, applications, or automated workflows.\nExperience developing technology products or platforms in the sports industry, particularly those involving live scoring, player statistics, sports data, or fan engagement.\nExperience working with sports statistics, real-time data feeds, or data visualization.\nExperience developing digital products or technology solutions for media, entertainment, broadcasting, or content distribution.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive salary and benefits package, including 401(k) with company match, unlimited PTO, and generous medical subsidy for employees and their spouses or qualified domestic partners.\nOpportunities to work closely with top industry professionals.\nA dynamic and collaborative work environment.\nUnrivaled is an equal opportunity organization. All qualified individuals will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, ancestry, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected under applicable federal, state or local law.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489690375": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. develops imaging systems and software that support professionals working in medical, clinical, and scientific environments. The company’s work brings together technology, imaging, and practical application to help customers capture, manage, and understand visual information. Canfield’s teams collaborate across disciplines to create and support solutions used in settings where reliability, usability, and thoughtful handling of data matter. Employees have the opportunity to contribute to products and services that serve specialized customer needs while working alongside colleagues with varied technical and professional expertise.\nAbout The Role\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. is seeking a Clinical PHP Web Developer, Level I to help build, enhance, and maintain web-based applications used in clinical and scientific workflows. This early-career position is suited to a developer who is motivated to grow, takes pride in producing dependable work, and enjoys collaborating with a focused, creative team. You will contribute to application development under the guidance of experienced colleagues, learning the company’s development practices and product environment as you take on increasing responsibility.\nThe ideal candidate communicates clearly, manages time effectively, and approaches work with curiosity and initiative. You should be comfortable asking questions, sharing progress, receiving feedback, and working through technical challenges methodically. This role offers the opportunity to strengthen your PHP development skills while contributing to applications that support real-world clinical processes. Attention to detail and a commitment to delivering maintainable, user-conscious solutions are important to success.\nQualifications\nQualified candidates will have foundational experience with PHP and a strong interest in developing web applications. Familiarity with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, relational databases, and SQL is valuable. Candidates should understand basic programming concepts, including variables, functions, data structures, debugging, and object-oriented development, and be willing to build on that knowledge in a collaborative setting. Experience with version control, such as Git, and awareness of software development life-cycle practices are also helpful.\nApplicants should demonstrate clear written and verbal communication, organization, reliable time management, and the ability to prioritize tasks. A self-motivated approach, sound problem-solving habits, attention to detail, and openness to feedback are essential. The successful candidate will be eager to learn, take ownership of assigned work, and contribute positively to a team. Education or practical experience in computer science, software development, or a related field may be beneficial.\nResponsibilities\nDevelop, test, troubleshoot, and maintain PHP-based web application features in accordance with project requirements and established development practices. Work with team members to clarify functionality, review requirements, and break assignments into manageable tasks. Write readable, maintainable code and help identify opportunities to improve application quality, usability, and performance. Investigate reported issues, reproduce problems, and assist with implementing and verifying appropriate fixes.\nCollaborate with developers, project stakeholders, and other colleagues to support reliable delivery. Participate in code reviews, team discussions, and testing activities, applying feedback to improve your work. Document relevant technical changes and communicate status, questions, and potential blockers in a timely manner. Follow applicable procedures for handling application data and contribute to a careful, quality-focused development process.\nBenefits\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. offers the opportunity to develop your technical skills while contributing to work in a specialized clinical and scientific technology environment. Team collaboration, practical assignments, and guidance from experienced colleagues can support continued professional growth. Compensation, benefits, and other employment details are determined by the position’s location and applicable company policies and will be shared during the hiring process.\nEqual Opportunity\nCanfield Scientific, Inc. is committed to providing equal employment opportunities. Employment decisions are made in accordance with applicable laws and without discrimination on the basis of protected characteristics. The company encourages qualified applicants with diverse backgrounds and experiences to apply. Reasonable accommodations are available during the application and interview process for individuals who need them.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490323871": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T01:31:28.213073+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We are looking for a software engineer with Django and Python Programming Development Skills. Our ideal Python developer will join us with a solid understanding of the language, a solid understanding of common frameworks, a drive to keep up to date with development trends, strong organizational skills, and an ability to learn quickly. Experience with machine learning and Google cloud is a huge plus!\nResponsibilities\nWrite reusable and efficient code.\nEnsure and implement balancing, usability, and automation.\nImplement data protection methods and implement low-latency performance applications.\nIntegrate user-facing elements with server-side logic and data storage solutions.\nIntegrate data storage solutions which may include databases, key-value stores, etc.\nCollaborate with the team to provide technical solutions and implement new software features.\nKnowledge of scrappy development.\nCommunicate with clients and team members.\nRequirements\nAt least a bachelor’s degree in CS/SE/IT.\nAt least 2-3 years of Python experience and frameworks such as Django and Scrappy.\nExperience working in Google Cloud Platform, Google Cloud Compute Engine, Google Cloud Storage, and Virtual Machine configurations using a Linux environment.\nFamiliarity with some ORM libraries.\nAble to integrate multiple data sources and databases into one system.\nUnderstanding of server-side temptation language, multi-process architecture, and limitations of Python.\nFamiliar with Selenium and other browser automation tools.\nStrong knowledge of fundamental design principles of an application, user authentication, and authorization between multiple systems, servers, and environments.\nSolid unit test and debugging skills.\nShould be able to work on multi-threaded applications.\nDistinguish between multiple delivery platforms.\nHands-on experience with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, NodeJs, and MySQL.\nExperience in Mongo dB would be a plus.\nGood communication skills.\nThe company offers a very good salary package with an excellent office environment. Also, paid holidays and recreational activities, indoor games, and a friendly environment. The company also offers Annual Bonuses and Appraisals depending on performance. Hoboetech believes in Growth, Promotion, recognition, and rewards. So apply with full confidence and show us your expertise for us to take care of your future.\nBenefits.\nMedical\nGaming Arena\nAppraisals\nProvident Fund\nBonuses\nIncentives\nDinners\nRoad Trips\nPaid Holidays\nInflation Petrol Allowance\nJob Category: IT & Telecommunication\nJob Type: Full Time\nJob Location: lahore\nApply for this position\nFull Name *\nEmail *\nPhone *\nBio *\nUpload CV/Resume *Allowed Type(s): .pdf, .doc, .docx\nBy using this form you agree with the storage and handling of your data by this website. *",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4434152039": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Canonical is a leading provider of open source software and operating systems to the global enterprise and technology markets. Our platform, Ubuntu, is very widely used in breakthrough enterprise initiatives such as public cloud, data science, AI, engineering innovation, and IoT. Our customers include the world's leading public cloud and silicon providers, and industry leaders in many sectors. The company is a pioneer of global distributed collaboration, with 1200+ colleagues in 75+ countries and very few office-based roles. Teams meet two to four times yearly in person, in interesting locations around the world, to align on strategy and execution.\nThe company is founder-led, profitable, and growing.\nWe are hiring a Software Engineer to develop, test and release improvements to the Ubuntu on public clouds.\nThe quality and stability of the Ubuntu is critically important, since it's available on every public cloud. You’ll work with teams across Canonical working on Ubuntu team, alongside major cloud partners to develop, test and release improvements to the Ubuntu cloud images. You will also be a voice in communication with our users, ensuring their needs are met.\nThis role requires quality-oriented software engineering in Python and a focus on software interoperability over a vast range of target releases and environments. Excellent Python skills are a key requirement, with previous contributions to open source Python projects being an advantage. This role involves creating and managing Ubuntu images; therefore, experience in configuring apt, and knowledge of deb packaging and general system administration is advantageous in this role.\nApplicants should be passionate about the Ubuntu project and its values and about building tools that are used by millions of people around the world. A personal interest and emphasis on quality, thinking of edge cases, ease of use, documentation, and careful community coordination is important. Ubuntu is used for all kinds of users, from mission-critical environments to hobbyist Ubuntu users; applicants should be ready to work with the whole spectrum of end users and help guide engineering best practices with all of them in mind.\nThe role entails\nCollaborate proactively with a distributed team\nWrite high quality code, with unit and functional tests, to create new features\nDebug issues and produce high quality code to fix them\nReview code produced by other engineers\nDiscuss ideas and investigate to find good solutions\nWork from home, with global travel 2 to 4 weeks per year for internal and external events\nWhat we are looking for in you\nYou love technology and working with brilliant people\nYou are curious, flexible, articulate, and accountable\nYou value soft skills and are passionate, enterprising, thoughtful, and self-motivated\nYou have a Bachelor’s or equivalent in Computer Science, STEM or similar degree\nYou have extensive experience with Python on Linux\nYou have interest in and experience with two or more of the following: Ubuntu Linux systems administration, continuous integration, end-system contract management, Debian packaging, working with public or on premise clouds\nBonus points if you have experience engaging with the open source community\nWhat We Offer Colleagues\nWe consider geographical location, experience, and performance in shaping compensation worldwide. We revisit compensation annually (and more often for graduates and associates) to ensure we recognize outstanding performance. In addition to base pay, we offer a performance-driven annual bonus or commission. We provide all team members with additional benefits which reflect our values and ideals. We balance our programs to meet local needs and ensure fairness globally.\nDistributed work environment with twice-yearly team sprints in person\nPersonal learning and development budget of USD 2,000 per year\nAnnual compensation review\nRecognition rewards\nAnnual holiday leave\nMaternity and paternity leave\nTeam Member Assistance Program & Wellness Platform\nOpportunity to travel to new locations to meet colleagues\nPriority Pass and travel upgrades for long-haul company events\nAbout Canonical\nCanonical is a pioneering tech firm at the forefront of the global move to open source. As the company that publishes Ubuntu, one of the most important open-source projects and the platform for AI, IoT, and the cloud, we are changing the world of software. We recruit on a global basis and set a very high standard for people joining the company. We expect excellence; in order to succeed, we need to be the best at what we do. Most colleagues at Canonical have worked from home since our inception in 2004. Working here is a step into the future and will challenge you to think differently, work smarter, learn new skills, and raise your game.\nCanonical is an equal opportunity employer\nWe are proud to foster a workplace free from discrimination. Diversity of experience, perspectives, and background create a better work environment and better products. Whatever your identity, we will give your application fair consideration.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4453262125": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Overview\nDeepgram is bringing the world’s most natural interface, voice, to the technology we use every day. Our speech models and real-time infrastructure power AI systems that keep up with the way people actually speak. More than 5,000 organizations run conversational voice AI on Deepgram in production, including Twilio, Cloudflare, Sierra, Decagon, Vapi, Cresta, Granola, and Jack in the Box.\nThe Deepgram Voice Agent Platform brings together speech-to-text, text-to-speech and speech-to-speech, with voice-native foundation models available through cloud APIs or self-hosted and on-premises deployments. Built for accuracy, low latency and cost efficiency, Deepgram makes high-quality voice experiences practical to build and run at scale. More than 650,000 developers have used Deepgram to process more than 200,000 years of audio. Every day, more of the world’s conversations with AI run on our models.\nOperating Principles:\nDeepgram is a research company that productizes as fast as possible. Four Operating Principles shape how we think, decide, and work together:\nCompress before you communicate. You think it through first, then lead with the bottom line.\nResist entropy. You question what already exists before adding more process or tools.\nSolve the category. You fix recurring problems at the source, not one case at a time.\nWork at the frontier. You go after problems no one has solved yet.\nWe look for people who already work this way, and these principles shape how we grow and evaluate our team.\nAI-First by Default\nWe build AI that millions of people talk to, and we run the company the same way. AI is how we centralize work here, and is core to how we operate.\nThat means more than using the tools. We expect you to:\nBuild, not just use. Design your own workflows and agents, and use AI to remove whole categories of work instead of doing the same work faster.\nOwn the output. AI can speed up the work. It doesn’t make anyone less accountable for it. You understand, verify, and stand behind everything you share, including what an agent produces for you.\nSpend the time you get back at the frontier. The capacity AI creates goes toward problems no one has solved yet.\nKeep pace. Models and tools change every month, and so will your work. You adopt what’s new quickly and drop what no longer earns its place.\nWe judge AI by what it helps you deliver and whether you stand behind the result, not by how often you use it. In interviews, expect to walk us through a workflow you built and where you drew the line between AI and your own judgment.\nStaff Web Engineer Marketing\nAbout The Role\nDeepgram builds foundational voice AI and deepgram.com is where the world meets it. The site is our digital front door, showcasing our products, brand moments, and pricing information, and it drives the company's self-serve revenue.\nWe're hiring a Staff Web Engineer to own the site's code for the long haul. Deepgram.com is entering its next chapter. We are fully refreshing the experience top to bottom. You'll be the person who knows the site inside out. You'll own the repo, the architecture, the Sanity environments, and the QA bar — and act as the code-review gate for day-to-day page and content work. The team is small but scaling. You will be working on the Web team reporting into the Head of Brand & Awareness and closely collaborating with our Senior Web Manager, product, marketing, sales, and external development partners.\nMost critically, as an AI company, you must be AI-native. Agents and AI tooling are your go-to in how you choose to build, review, and QA. We are aiming to build a machine-first, voice-first site experience. It’s an exciting time to join the web team.\nWhat you'll do\nOwn the deepgram.com codebase end to end — the Next.js application (front and back end), the GitHub repo, branching and CI/CD, and code review\nOptimize and maintain Sanity CMS architecture — schemas, the reusable module library, the staging and production environments and publishing workflow\nRun the global design system, component library, Vercel platform and spearhead AI integrations. Experienced with global CSS systems.\nBuild and run the site's QA program — starting with a well-structured and scalable staging environment that keeps a marketing site launch-ready at all times\nLead internationalization and localization efforts — language-locale URL and routing architecture, hreflang, and the path from i18n plumbing to localized (l10n) content\nAssist in technical SEO — site architecture, redirects, Core Web Vitals — with on-page SEO executed by content partners inside your review gate\nEnsure LLM discoverability (AEO) — the site's structured data, metadata, and content architecture must serve answer engines as well as people\nTechnical infrastructure for experimentation — develop the mechanisms to support the site's experimentation program\nMarketing Ops partnership — implementation of forms, gated content, and attribution instrumentation (GTM, GA4, HubSpot)\nCybersecurity posture — maintain security and run routine safety audits across dependencies and scripts\nHigh-velocity shipping — ship complex site improvements and launch campaign pages in a product-driven atmosphere\nAI-native workflow — use agents in your daily build process and create tooling for safe marketing publishing\nWe are looking for candidates with:\nMarketing web development background — ownership of marketing sites, not just product surfaces\nEnterprise repository ownership: branching strategy, CI/CD, and a strong code-review culture\nHeadless CMS architecture — Next.js with Sanity strongly preferred\nModern React ecosystem for the web\nVercel as a production platform\nAI-native development — ability to demonstrate concrete use of AI agents and tooling in your workflow\nHigh level of ownership & accountability — a hand raiser who’s ready to join an ambitious team and company\nTechnical leadership — directing or reviewing the work of agency developers\nOur ideal candidates also have:\nPrior experience with internationalization (i18n/l10n): URL architecture, locale routing, and multi-region infrastructure\nFamiliarity with A/B testing on production marketing sites\nInterest in voice AI and the future of voice-interactive web experiences\nNotice : We're aware of individuals impersonating Deepgram recruiters. All legitimate Deepgram recruiting communication comes from an @ deepgram.com email address. If you've received a message claiming to be Deepgram, please forward it to careers@deepgram.com.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4472049827": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "The MongoDB Developer Tools team is a diverse group of contributors working together to help our users manage MongoDB at global scale. This includes building tools for MongoDB Atlas: our database as a service offering and fastest growing product which allows users to deploy fault-tolerant, globally distributed MongoDB clusters in just minutes.\nWe're seeking an experienced Software Engineer to join our Developer Tools Team within the Database Experience department. The team is responsible for tools which allow users to interact with their data and to understand the health and performance of their MongoDB deployments. The Developer Tools Team works on a variety of APIs and customer-facing UIs empowering MongoDB users to interact with their stored data, whether that’s on desktop via MongoDB Compass or in the browser via Atlas Data Explorer.\nThis role is fully remote for a candidate based in the United States with US citizenship.\nWe're looking for someone who\nIs a full stack engineer with a willingness to take on both frontend tasks and backend tasks\nExperience working with TypeScript, React, and Node.js\nHas experience with the design and architecture of a modern, scalable, high availability web application\nHas experience working with databases\nEnjoys collaboration and being part of a team\nIs approachable, curious, and intellectually honest\nWould enjoy chasing down difficult problems in a distributed environment\nAlways strives to expand their knowledge\nNice to Haves\nKnowledge of database internals and tuning mechanisms, particularly indexing\nExperience working with websocket based client to server communication\nFamiliarity with developing and supporting microservice based architectures using Kubernetes\nAbout MongoDB\nMongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.\nWith offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including 75% of the Fortune 100 and AI-native startups, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.\nOur compass at MongoDB is our Leadership Commitment, guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.\nTo drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys. Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB, and help us make an impact on the world!\nMongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.\nMongoDB, Inc. provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type and makes all hiring decisions without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.\nReq ID: 2273494846\nMongoDB’s base salary range for this role is posted below. Compensation at the time of offer is unique to each candidate and based on a variety of factors such as skill set, experience, qualifications, and work location. Salary is one part of MongoDB’s total compensation and benefits package. Other benefits for eligible employees may include: equity, participation in the employee stock purchase program, flexible paid time off, 20 weeks fully-paid gender-neutral parental leave, fertility and adoption assistance, 401(k) plan, mental health counseling, access to transgender-inclusive health insurance coverage, and health benefits offerings. Please note, the base salary range listed below and the benefits in this paragraph are only applicable to U.S.-based candidates.\nMongoDB’s base salary range for this role in the U.S. is:\n$85,000—$230,000 USD",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4472215481": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Who We Are\nAt Robert Half, we’re driven by innovation and a passion for building technology that makes a difference. We’re looking for a Software Engineer I to help design, develop, and support applications that power our global business operations — from finance and HR systems to modern web platforms.\nAs part of our forward-thinking engineering team, you’ll work in an environment that values curiosity and continuous learning. We’re integrating Generative AI and intelligent automation into our development practices to enhance creativity, accelerate delivery, and improve how we solve real business problems.\nYou’ll have the chance to contribute to meaningful projects, collaborate with experienced professionals, and grow your skills through hands-on experience in modern tools and technologies.\nWhat You’ll Do\nAnalyze and resolve basic production issues following department guidelines and troubleshooting practices.\nProvide Level I development and application support.\nDevelop individual modules or components in a larger system architecture.\nModify and/or enhance existing components of a small scale with guidance from a supervisor or senior engineer.\nPerform unit test planning and execution for own code.\nExecute integration testing within project scope.\nDesign individual modules or components of limited scope in larger system designs.\nCollaborate on AI-assisted software development tasks, leveraging Generative AI tools to improve coding efficiency, generate test cases, or assist in documentation.\nSupport small-scale proof-of-concept projects involving GenAI APIs, prompt engineering, or AI-driven automation within the software stack.\nParticipate in continuous learning initiatives related to AI technologies, including model APIs, embeddings, and responsible AI use.\nWhat You’ll Need\nBachelor's degree in engineering or related field, or 2+ years’ equivalent experience in a related field within a medium-to-large IT organization.\nCertifications: Microsoft Tech, PeopleSoft Tech, Java Tech, OpenSource Tech.\nRequires no previous professional experience.\n1+ years’ experience with a programming or scripting language (C#, Java, JavaScript, SQL).\n1+ years’ experience writing/modifying programs for small to mid-size applications.\n1+ years’ experience administering and/or configuring an application.\nBasic knowledge of the software development lifecycle (SDLC).\nBasic knowledge of n-tiered architecture.\nBasic understanding of database concepts.\nExposure to Microsoft container, Open Source container, and Java platforms.\nFamiliarity with cloud-based AI services (e.g., Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, or Google Vertex AI) and RESTful API integration with LLMs preferred.\nFoundational understanding of Generative AI and awareness of ethical AI practices.\nAbility to interact and communicate with customers of varying levels of expertise.\nAbility to communicate technical information to non-technical users.\nAbility to communicate business processes to technical resources.\nAbility to create simple process flow diagrams or flowcharts that demonstrate business or system process flow.\nAbility to gather requirements and create test plans.\nThe typical annual salary range for this position is shown below and is negotiable depending upon experience and location.\n$68,000.00 - $102,000.00\nWe offer exceptional earning potential and a competitive benefits package, including group health insurance benefits (medical, vision, dental), FSA and HSA healthcare accounts, life and accident insurance, adoption and fertility assistance, paid parental leave of up to 6 weeks, and short/long term disability. Robert Half provides paid time off for vacation, personal needs, and sick time. The amount of Choice Time Off (CTO) our people receive varies based on their years of service and is pro-rated based on the hours worked per week. A new hire earns up to 17 days of CTO per calendar year. Our people also receive up to 11 paid holidays per calendar year. We also offer the opportunity to contribute to our company 401(k) savings and investment plan or deferred compensation plan (if eligible), with an employer match of 100% on the first 3% of your contributions for eligible employees. Learn more at https://roberthalfbenefits.com.\nRobert Half Inc. is an Equal Opportunity Employer. M/F/Disability/Veteran\nAs part of Robert Half’s Corporate Services facility employment process, any offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check.\nOur recruiters use their expertise and may utilize AI to help with their evaluation of candidates.\nRobert Half is committed to being an equal employment employer offering opportunities to all job seekers, including individuals with disabilities. If you believe you need a reasonable accommodation in order to search for a job opening or to apply for a position, please contact us by sending an email to HRSolutions@roberthalf.com or call 1.855.744.6947 for assistance.\nIn Your Email Please Include The Following\nThe specific accommodation requested to complete the employment application.\nThe location(s) (city, state) to which you would like to apply.\nFor positions located in San Francisco, CA: Robert Half will consider qualified applicants with criminal histories in a manner consistent with the requirements of the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.\nFor positions located in Los Angeles County, CA: Robert Half will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records in accordance with the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers and the California Fair Chance Act.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482124719": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Position\nForward Deployed Engineers sit inside the client’s problem, not next to it. You embed with an enterprise team, find the work that actually warrants AI, architect the system, build it, and stay long enough to make it survive contact with production.\nThis is a three-way role: consultant, operator, engineer. You should be as comfortable pressure-testing a business case with a COO or VP of Engineering as you are diagnosing why retrieval quality collapsed after a data refresh. The people who succeed here can hold a discovery conversation on Monday and ship what they scoped on Thursday.\nOn this track, your edge is data, retrieval, and model behavior: you make agents trustworthy by getting the data, context, and evaluation right.\nWe work with regulated industries and Fortune 500 clients who have AI mandates, real constraints, and low tolerance for demos that don’t hold up.\nHow We Approach The Work\nFDEs are trusted to shape the solution, not only deliver it. Every engagement calls for architect-level judgment:\nReframes the request. Treats “we need an agent for X” as a hypothesis, not a spec.\nDecomposes the problem. Outcome → process → decisions → data → systems → actors → constraints — before choosing technology.\nChooses the intervention. Remove, simplify, traditional software, automation, LLM, RAG, agent, or multi-agent — and defends why.\nOwns the architecture decision. Documents trade-offs (ADRs), sets success metrics, pushes back on scope that won’t deliver value.\nConsultative Discovery\nClients rarely arrive with a fully formed problem, and the FDE’s first contribution is helping them see it clearly. You lead discovery with genuine curiosity, moving the conversation from stated requirements to underlying needs, and you build credibility through the depth of your understanding rather than the breadth of your pitch.\nUncovers business drivers. What outcome matters, what it’s worth, why now, and what happens if nothing changes.\nUncovers personal drivers. What each stakeholder is measured on, what they’re worried about, and what a win looks like for them individually.\nSurfaces constraints early. Security, compliance, data access, budget, skills, politics, timelines — the things that kill projects in month two.\nAligns stakeholders. Spots conflicting goals between business, engineering, and risk, and brings them to a shared definition of success.\nAsks strategic questions. Follows the answer with “why,” “how do you know,” and “what happens today when…” — without interrogating. Clients leave the conversation understanding their own problem better.\nEarns authority through depth. Credibility comes from the quality of the questions and the insight in the playback, not from pitching technology.\nWhat You'll Do\nDiscover. Run workshops and process discovery with business, data, and engineering stakeholders. Assess data readiness honestly. Separate genuine AI problems from workflow problems wearing an AI costume.\nStructure the process and the spec. For any business process being automated, map the current state, decision points, data inputs, and exceptions, then turn it into specifications that both people and AI systems can execute against reliably.\nArchitect & design. Design agentic systems end to end with emphasis on context and retrieval architecture — data sourcing, chunking, embeddings, hybrid search, reranking, permissions-aware retrieval, knowledge graphs where warranted — plus orchestration, MCP/tool integration, guardrails, and human-in-the-loop checkpoints.\nBuild. Ship working systems — agents, retrieval services, evaluation tooling, and the data flows that feed them. Prototypes that prove value in weeks, not slideware.\nEngineer the delivery system. Own CI/CD for what you build, extended to AI: prompt and context versioning, eval suites that run in the pipeline and gate releases.\nOperate (Day 2). Own what happens after launch — eval harnesses, groundedness and retrieval metrics, observability and tracing, cost and latency management, drift, and the handoff that lets the client’s team run it without you.\nConsult. Present to and defend decisions in front of CTOs, VPs of Engineering, CDOs, and business leadership. Quantify impact in their terms. Support pre-sales scoping and proposal work when the deal calls for it.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with core proficiency in Python (or TypeScript/Node.js).\nHas shipped at least one agentic AI solution, LLM workflow, or RAG architecture to a production environment.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nDemonstrated hands-on experience using AI developer tools (such as Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, or OpenAI Codex) in daily workflows.\nTrack record of leading client-facing discovery calls to translate unstructured business requirements into technical architectures.\nHands-on experience designing and integrating RESTful APIs, microservices, or event-driven architectures.\nExperience building agentic systems using orchestration frameworks or APIs such as LangGraph, LangChain, n8n, Model Context Protocol (MCP), or direct LLM APIs.\nProven experience taking full end-to-end technical ownership of features from discovery to deployment.\nAbility to work through new and difficult issues and contribute to libraries as needed.\nAbility to create and maintain continuous integration and delivery of applications.\nForensic attention to detail.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nExperience working on Agile / Scrum teams.\nMeaningful experience working on large, complex systems.\nAbility to take extreme ownership over your work. Every day is a challenge to ensure you are performing to the expectations you and your team have agreed upon.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients, and dedicate yourself to delivering on the commitments you and your team make to them.\nStrong Plus\nProduction AI operations (Day 2): eval harnesses, observability and tracing, cost and token economics, drift, debugging non-deterministic systems.\nPrompt- and eval-level regression testing running in CI and gating releases.\nDelivery in regulated environments (financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing).\nPre-sales support: discovery calls, SOW and estimate shaping, technical proposal defense.\nProcess mining, operations analysis, or transformation consulting background.\nClient enablement and training — building the client team’s capability, not just the system.\nPrior consulting or agency environment; comfort with ambiguity and multiple accounts.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486161894": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Zyte, we don't just collect web data—we solve complex web data challenges at scale. We are a globally distributed team that is bold, curious, and dedicated to building innovative ways to deliver clean, reliable web data from across the internet.\nData is our passion: We unlock access to open web data, empowering organizations—from startups to global enterprises—to power competitive intelligence, analytics, and AI pipelines\nRemote-first culture: Work from anywhere in the world. With over 260 Zytans across 33 countries, our strength comes from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and skills\nEngineering excellence: We love diving deep into complex code bases, evaluating emerging technologies, and pushing technical boundaries. If you thrive on creative problem-solving and reliably delivering production-grade solutions, you will fit right in\nEstablished system design framework: We systematically analyze functional and product requirements alongside architectural trade-offs to make informed, sustainable design decisions\nReal-world distributed systems challenges: Tackle rare engineering problems in custom networking, high-throughput streaming, and large-scale orchestration under real-world operational constraints\nStrong product ownership: Work on a profitable, market-leading platform with dedicated time and resources allocated for architectural research and strategic feature engineering\nWhy This Role?\nZyte API fetches the web through a ladder of routes: plain HTTP, headless browsers, and, for the hardest targets, Edge—our own residential network of real devices. Edge is the tier that must succeed when everything else has failed. Today, a Rust peer on residential Windows PCs long-polls a single command-and-control service (CNC) over mTLS gRPC; CNC schedules fetches onto peers, runs a CONNECT proxy gateway, owns geo-routing, per-site cooldowns, and bandwidth quotas. It must grow from thousands of nodes to tens of millions of requests a day with rock-solid reliability.\nThe Edge Platform squad owns the control plane and data plane of this residential stack across Windows, Android, and Linux. The next step is building a proper Fleet Manager: a control plane with provider adapters (volunteer PCs, mobile-IP device farms, self-hosted nodes), a reconciler, rollout control, and metrics export sitting beside CNC as the data plane. You will design and operate that system—handling the scheduling, networking, proxying, and reliability work that turns residential devices into infrastructure other squads depend on. You will work directly with the Team Lead, a Principal Engineer, and partner engineering squads across Zyte.\nWhat You'll Do\nScale the data plane. Evolve CNC from a single-replica service into a horizontally scalable fetch scheduler: node selection that respects geo, site cooldowns, jail and per-peer quotas while avoiding detectable patterns, at 50-100M requests per day\nBuild the Fleet Manager control plane. Design and ship the inventory, health, configuration and software-rollout plane for the fleet: provider adapters, a reconciler, a rollout controller and an exporter to BigQuery, so a second device provider can be onboarded without bespoke scripts\nOwn the proxy path. Operate and improve the CONNECT proxy gateway and session handling on the edge, and work with the API squad on IP reputation, proxy leases and request scheduling so Edge slots cleanly into the platform's proxy plane\nEngineer the networking. mTLS gRPC between control plane and peers, long-poll and streaming semantics over unreliable residential links, NAT and carrier-grade NAT behaviour, and bandwidth accounting that is correct under contention\nMake it reliable. Define SLOs for availability, success and latency of the Edge route; build the metrics on peer count, drop-off and bandwidth that hold us and our supply partners accountable; run blue/green rollouts of CNC and peers safely\nShare production ownership. Take part in the squad's on-call rotation, lead incident post-mortems and turn operational lessons into platform improvements\nRaise the bar. Write RFDs for scheduling, fleet management and failover; review designs across the squad; and bring distributed-systems rigour (consistency, backpressure, idempotency, blast radius) to a young codebase\nRequirements\nWho You Are\n5+ years of production Rust experience, shipping and operating services you own end to end\nDistributed systems: you have designed and run schedulers, control planes or stateful services at scale, and can reason about consistency, partitions, backpressure and idempotency without a whiteboard\nDeep networking: TCP, TLS and HTTP at the handshake and packet level, gRPC and long-lived connections across NAT and lossy links, and what a client looks like on the wire\nProxy expertise: you have built or operated forward proxies, proxy gateways or residential/ISP proxy infrastructure, and understand IP reputation, session stickiness and pool health\nOps and reliability experience: SLOs and error budgets, observability you built yourself, production incidents you led, and comfort with being on call\nCross-platform awareness: comfortable with Rust running on Windows, Linux and Android targets, and with FFI boundaries when the data plane needs them\nAsync communication: strong written communication for a globally distributed, remote-first environment\nCurious problem solver: you like finding out why a system behaves the way it does under load, and fixing the cause rather than the symptom\nOur Tech Stack\nLanguages: Rust (tokio, tonic), C++ (Cronet) at the peer boundary; Python and Java in the services we integrate with\nProtocols: gRPC and protobuf over mTLS, HTTP CONNECT proxying, the Chromium network stack and our own browserless HTTP client\nInfrastructure: GCP and Kubernetes for the control plane, Terraform, blue/green deployments; multi-cloud (OCI, GCP) and data centres (Hetzner, Servers.com) across the wider platform\nData & Messaging: Valkey, BigQuery, Confluent Kafka\nMonitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry\nBonus Points\nMobile or desktop Rust: experience shipping Rust on Android, Windows or macOS, or binding Rust to C/C++ via FFI\nFleet or device management: reconcilers, rollout controllers, IoT or volunteer-computing fleets\nAnti-bot and fingerprinting: understanding of how TLS, HTTP and IP signals are used to classify traffic\nWeb scraping & crawling experience: familiarity with the technical challenges of large-scale web data extraction\nOpen source contributions: history of contributing to Rust, networking or distributed-systems open-source projects\nWhy Join Us?\nImpact at scale: Build the residential network tier behind web-scale data pipelines for top-tier global enterprises\nAutonomy and flexibility: Enjoy a genuine remote-first culture with flexible working hours and high organizational trust\nContinuous innovation: Solve emerging, complex technical challenges as AI and web data extraction rapidly evolve\nGlobal community: Collaborate with a passionate, diverse team of distributed systems engineers and data specialists across the world\nIf you are a Rust engineer who wants to turn tens of thousands of residential devices into dependable infrastructure, we would love to hear from you. Join us in building the fleet behind web data extraction at Zyte.\nBenefits\nBy joining the Zyte team, you will:\nBecome part of a self-motivated, progressive, multi-cultural team\nHave the freedom and flexibility to work from where you do your best work\nAttend conferences and meet with team members from across the globe\nWork with cutting-edge open source technologies and tools",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487447757": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Purpose\n- Key Result Areas\n- Uses his/her technical expertise and experience to contribute to all sprint events (planning, refinements, retrospectives, demos)\n- Consults with the team about what is needed to fulfil the functional and non-functional requirements of the IT product to be developed\n- Develops the IT product, performs the unit test in line with the customer’s wishes and IT area’s internal ambitions and reviews colleagues’ IT products.\n- Designs, builds and tests IT products (functional, performance, resilience and security tests) and automates them.\n- Performs Life Cycle Management (including decommissioning) for IT products under management\n- Improves the Continuous Delivery process\n- Resolves incidents and problems relating to IT products under management (including stack)\n- Sets up the IT environment, deploys the IT product on the IT infrastructure and implements the required changes\n- Sets up monitoring of IT product usage by the customer\nOperating Environment, Framework and Boundaries, Working Relationships- The Front End developer is responsible for transforming the design and the product vision into working products and will directly influence how users will interact with the system. The Front End developer works hard to stay on top of fast changing technology and invests a lot of energy in learning new tricks. They are not only caught up on industry trends in client development frameworks but also know what the near future will bring. A love for clean interfaces and a passion for great user experiences goes without saying\n- Works within a multidisciplinary team or in an environment in which multidisciplinary teamwork is carried out.\n- Is primarily responsible for the production (or technical\nconfiguration) of software applications.\n- The range of tasks includes the following:\n- the analysis and design of the application(or the technical configuration);\n- coding applications and/or package integration in one programming languages, scripting languages and frameworks:\n- HTML, CSS/LESS/SCSS/etc., JavaScript, and responsive design\n- Mobile development experience with either native or web-to-native tooling and frameworks\n- JavaScript frameworks and libraries specifically React\n- Understanding of RESTful APIs and how use them in practice\n- Knowledge of Object-Oriented programing\n- Continuous Delivery (Compile, Build, Package, Deploy);\n- Test-Driven Development (TDD) and test automation (e.g. regression, functional and integration tests); debugging and profiling;\n- software configuration management and version control.\n- Be an active participant in grooming and planning, to ensure that acceptance criteria are clear\n- Sit together with designers, SMEs and Product Owner while user stories are developed, bringing input\n- Work in an agile/scrum environment, meeting sprint commitments and contributing to the agile process\n- Maintain traceability of testing activities\nProblem Solving\n- Ability to handle challenges and multi-task, in a high pressure & demanding environment\nDecision Making Authority & Responsibility\n- Take ownership of key decisions, ensuring alignment with organizational goals and stakeholder expectations\nKnowledge, Skills and Experience\n- Past experience as a frontend developer building modern JavaScript-based web applications\n- Expert experience with HTML, CSS/LESS/SCSS/etc., JavaScript, and responsive design\n- Mobile development experience with either native or web-to-native tooling and frameworks\n- Experience using JavaScript frameworks and libraries specifically React\n- Understanding of RESTful APIs and how use them in practice\n- Knowledge of Object-Oriented programing\n- Ability to write effective unit, integration, and end-user automation tests\n- Strong understanding of Agile methodologies\n- Experience as a Developer on a cross-functional agile team preferred\n- Strong communication skills with ability to communicate complex technical concepts and align organization on decisions\n- Sound problem-solving skills with the ability to quickly process complex information and present it clearly and simply\n- Utilizes team collaboration to create innovative solutions efficiently\n- Passionate about technology and excited about the impact of emerging /\ndisruptive technologies\n- Wants to unleash inner self-starter and work in an environment that fosters\nentrepreneurial minds\n- Believes in culture of transparency and trust\n- Open to learning new ideas outside scope or knowledge skillset\n- Problem Analysis\n- Professional expertise/market focus",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487850358": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Description\nLeidos is seeking a Junior Full Stack Software Engineer to work remotely supporting the DHMSM contract. The DHMSM program provides modernization of Electronic Health Record (EHR) capabilities for the Department of Defense along with Virtual Health capabilities. The team is seeking candidates for the engineering team to support defining, implementing, deploying and sustaining the Virtual Health capabilities.\nPrimary Responsibilities\nDevelop and support containerized microservices within a Kubernetes cluster\nJava development of microservices to implement new capabilities or enhance existing services\nJavaScript/Typescript development of UI capabilities\nFull stack implementation and support capabilities\nCreative problem solving of issues that arise in local and production environments\nOwn tasks through analysis, implementation, and production deployment\nWork closely with Operations team to implement features and work in environments\nSupport CI/CD automation related to services\nCreate adequate and understandable documentation for services\nCommunicate effectively across product, development, operations, and application security teams\nLeverage technical expertise and participate in the definition of new capabilities and the enhancement or troubleshooting of existing capabilities\nAbility to quickly ramp up on new technologies when encountered\nWork independently within a matrixed organization\nBasic Qualifications\nBS Degree and 1-4 years of prior relevant experience.\nUS Citizen with current US Government clearance; ability to obtain and maintain ADP2/IT2 Public Trust. Federal Government requirement.\nIn depth technical understanding and strong development experience with:\nJava (or similar Object-Oriented programming languages)\nJavaScript/Typescript/HTML/CSS\nExposure to:\nJavaScript / Typescript / HTML / CSS (and related UI frameworks like Angular/React)\nAWS (or similar cloud provider)\nLinux (RHEL or Debian/Ubuntu)\nScripting (Bash, Python)\nCI/CD automation (e.g. Gitlab, Jenkins)\nAutomated unit and integration testing (e.g. Junit, Jasmine, Selenium)\nStrong verbal and written communications skills, with an ability to express complex technical concepts in business terms\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and conceptual skills\nStrong interpersonal skills; ability to communicate and persuade at all management levels and thrive in a cross-functional environment\nRequirements interpretation and decomposition\nAgile software development (Kanban, Scrum), including testing\nPreferred Qualifications\nDevOps and operational support experience\nExperience with EHR system infrastructure architecture and implementation\nExperience with the following technologies is desired:\nSpring based microservices (or similar)\nREST API’s (JSON, XML)\nContainerization (Docker)\nContainer Orchestration (Kubernetes)\nInfrastructure as Code (Ansible, Terraform, Cloudformation)\nAWS Managed Services\nStatic code analysis & quality (e.g. Sonarqube, Sqale, JArchitect, Fortify)\nContainer/Artifact Registries (e.g. Nexus, Harbor)\nIf you're looking for comfort, keep scrolling. At Leidos, we outthink, outbuild, and outpace the status quo — because the mission demands it. We're not hiring followers. We're recruiting the ones who disrupt, provoke, and refuse to fail. Step 10 is ancient history. We're already at step 30 — and moving faster than anyone else dares.\nOriginal Posting\nNovember 10, 2026\nFor U.S. Positions: While subject to change based on business needs, Leidos reasonably anticipates that this job requisition will remain open for at least 3 days with an anticipated close date of no earlier than 3 days after the original posting date as listed above.\nPay Range\nPay Range $69,550.00 - $125,725.00\nThe Leidos pay range for this job level is a general guideline onlyand not a guarantee of compensation or salary. Additional factors considered in extending an offer include (but are not limited to) responsibilities of the job, education, experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity, alignment with market data, applicable bargaining agreement (if any), or other law.\nAbout Leidos\nLeidos is an industry and technology leader serving government and commercial customers with smarter, more efficient digital and mission innovations. Headquartered in Reston, Virginia, with 47,000 global employees, Leidos reported annual revenues of approximately $16.7 billion for the fiscal year ended January 3, 2025. For more information, visit www.Leidos.com.\nPay And Benefits\nPay and benefits are fundamental to any career decision. That's why we craft compensation packages that reflect the importance of the work we do for our customers. Employment benefits include competitive compensation, Health and Wellness programs, Income Protection, Paid Leave and Retirement. More details are available at www.leidos.com/careers/pay-benefits.\nSecuring Your Data\nBeware of fake employment opportunities using Leidos’ name. Leidos will never ask you to provide payment-related information during any part of the employment application process (i.e., ask you for money), nor will Leidos ever advance money as part of the hiring process (i.e., send you a check or money order before doing any work). Further, Leidos will only communicate with you through emails that are generated by the Leidos.com automated system – never from free commercial services (e.g., Gmail, Yahoo, Hotmail) or via WhatsApp, Telegram, etc. If you received an email purporting to be from Leidos that asks for payment-related information or any other personal information (e.g., about you or your previous employer), and you are concerned about its legitimacy, please make us aware immediately by emailing us at LeidosCareersFraud@leidos.com.\nIf you believe you are the victim of a scam, contact your local law enforcement and report the incident to the U.S. Federal Trade Commission.\nCommitment to Non-Discrimination\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, ethnicity, age, national origin, citizenship, religion, physical or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, pregnancy, family structure, marital status, ancestry, domestic partner status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran or military status, or any other basis prohibited by law. Leidos will also consider for employment qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with relevant laws.\n#Remote",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488069935": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Small businesses represent 99.9% of all companies, yet they're still forced to choose between clunky, outdated enterprise phone systems or their personal phones. This multi-billion dollar market has been overlooked for decades, left to cobble together solutions that slow them down instead of helping them grow.\nQuo is changing that. We bring calls, texts, and customer information together into one easy-to-use, AI-powered platform. We're not just building a phone system. We're setting a new standard for how businesses connect with their customers.\nDriven by our values, we move fast, build with determination, and obsess over delivering value to the businesses that have been underserved for far too long.\nToday, Quo is trusted by more than 120,000 companies and rated #1 in customer satisfaction on G2. We're backed by Y Combinator, Tiger Global, Craft Ventures, Slow Ventures, and other top-tier investors. It's safe to say we're onto something big.\nAbout The Role\nOur Foundations team sits between the cloud infrastructure and the product teams who build features. We build the patterns, libraries and backend capabilities the rest of Quo engineering builds on. When a change touches every team, it usually starts here.\nRight now that means leading our move from REST to GraphQL. Foundations is doing the first big pieces of the migration and creating the patterns and tools so every other team can finish their part on their own. After that, the work moves to whatever matters most across the org, like reworking how authentication and authorization work at Quo, or rethinking how we do search.\nAs a Staff Backend Engineer, you'll be hands-on and writing production code, working closely with the Foundations lead. You'll stay on one team but spend a lot of your time alongside other teams, helping them adopt a new pattern, writing code with them and making sure it works for their part of the product. This isn't a feature team role, and it isn't DevOps or SRE either. It's backend engineering whose impact shows up across the whole of Quo.\nSome Of The Things You’ll Do\nLead the technical work on our REST to GraphQL migration, building the core pieces yourself and the patterns that let every other team finish theirs.\nShape how our GraphQL architecture grows, including breaking one large graph into supergraphs and subgraphs that teams can own and change independently.\nHelp rework authentication and authorization across Quo, working directly with each team it touches and writing code alongside them.\nBuild reusable libraries and backend patterns that product engineers use every day as they ship features.\nDesign reliable, scalable backend systems that hold up as more and more businesses run on Quo.\nSet technical direction for foundational work, from search to API design, and bring other teams along through design docs, reviews and pairing.\nMentor engineers on Foundations and across the org, raising the bar for how backend work gets done at Quo.\nTech Stack & Tools\nNode and TypeScript on the backend\nEvent-driven microservices with Temporal and RabbitMQ at the centre\nKubernetes on AWS\nPostgres, MongoDB, Elasticsearch and Redis\nDatadog for observability\nWeb (React), iOS and Android clients on the other side of the API\nLanguage is not a filter. If you've built the right things in Go, Python, Java or anything else, we'd rather talk to you than to someone who knows Node but hasn't.\nAbout You\nYou write TypeScript every day and know it deeply. You're comfortable with its type system and the patterns that keep a large codebase healthy.\nYou've built and run GraphQL APIs in production, and ideally you've helped move a codebase from REST to GraphQL or led a similar API modernisation.\nYou're a strong backend engineer with a solid grasp of systems design, reliability and infrastructure, and you've built systems that scale.\nYou enjoy building things other engineers depend on, like shared libraries, patterns and platform capabilities, and you care about making them easy to use.\nYou can influence technical direction across teams, explain trade-offs clearly and get people on board without needing authority over them.\nYou like ownership and some ambiguity. You've worked somewhere with real users and real structure, whether that's a larger tech company or a scaling startup, and you want to make a visible difference here.\nYou're happiest writing code. This is a hands-on role, not a DevOps, SRE or developer productivity programme role.\nBonus Points If You\nHave worked on authentication and authorization, search or graph architecture.\nHave production and/or operational experience with GraphQL federation.\nHave worked across web, mobile and backend, even though this role is backend first.\nCompensation\nThe annual base salary range for this position is as follows, plus equity and benefits:\nSF Bay Area, Los Angeles, Seattle, Portland, Boston, New York, and Washington, DC Metro: $205,000 - $242,000 USD\nAll other US Locations: $186,000 - $217,000 USD\nCanada: $189,000 - $222,000 CAD\nThe ranges displayed reflect the target for new hire salaries, and within each range, individual pay is determined by your skills and experience, as well as relevant education. Your recruiter can share more and answer questions about the specific salary range during the hiring process.\nSalary is just one component of Quo’s total compensation package. Your total rewards package will include equity, extensive medical coverage, a monthly lifestyle stipend, and a flexible PTO policy.\nWho we are\nWe're a remote-first company with a culture of trust, autonomy, and action. As we rapidly grow, we're intentionally building communities in a handful of hub cities while continuing to hire great talent wherever they happen to live. If you're looking for a place to do your best work, we'd love to hear from you.\nAnd remember, there's no such thing as a 'perfect' candidate. We're looking for optimists with grit and determination, who are excited to face the challenges of a growing startup. Quo is the type of company where you can grow, and we encourage you to apply for this role even if you don't think you meet all the requirements.\nWe are committed to creating an inclusive and diverse work environment. It is important that you are able to bring your authentic self to work every day. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. #PostLI",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488249448": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description\nVector Viral develops Unity games, mobile apps, backend systems, multiplayer infrastructure, AI-powered solutions, blockchain applications, and digital products. We focus on scalable, high-performance solutions for games and apps across mobile and web platforms.\nRole Description\nRemote role for a Unity Backend Developer . Responsibilities include developing backend systems for Unity games and apps, multiplayer features, APIs, SDK ,cloud integration, gameplay systems, optimization, debugging, and maintaining and improve scalable architectures for live applications.\nQualifications\nStrong proficiency in Game Programming and Gameplay Programming\nExperience with Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) and general Programming practices\nUnderstanding of Game Design principles\nProblem-solving and debugging skills, with the ability to optimize performance\nProficiency with Unity or similar game engines\nFamiliarity with databases, authentication systems, and real-time networking websockets UDP/TCP\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field\nExperience with backend integration for multiplayer games\nSDK/Tools development experience for untiy game engine",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488261051": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We're hiring 10 Full-Stack Engineers at CCRIPT.\nLocation: On-site, Islamabad or Lahore\nHours: New York hours, full-time. That's 6 PM – 3 AM in Pakistan.\nPay: Salary on the 1st. Your share of client revenue on the 15th. That's Commissions.\nLevel: Mid to senior\nWe don't want people who only build to a ticket. We want engineers who can take a product from an idea to something real users depend on, and own all of it: the interface, the API, the database and the deploy.\nIf you've only ever worked on one side of the stack, this isn't for you. If you've shipped full products that people use every day, keep reading.\nWhat you'll do\n• Build and ship web products with TypeScript, React and Next.js on the front and Node.js on the back\n• Design data models and APIs, and work with Postgres\n• Build fast, clean, accessible interfaces that work on any screen\n• Integrate LLM APIs and AI features into real products\n• Deploy and run what you build with Docker, CI/CD and the cloud\n• Use AI tools (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, agents) every day to ship faster and better. We pay for them.\n• Own your features after launch: monitor them, fix what breaks and keep improving them\nWhat we're looking for\n• Mid to senior experience as a full-stack engineer, with products running in production\n• Strong TypeScript, React and Next.js, and Node.js on the server\n• Solid with SQL databases, ideally Postgres, and with designing APIs\n• You care about the details users notice: speed, polish and things that just work\n• Experience with Docker, CI/CD and a cloud like AWS\n• Experience building with LLM APIs is a big plus\n• You pick up new frameworks and tools fast\n• AI tools are already part of how you work\n• High ownership. You finish what you start and fix what's broken.\nThe basics\n• A 20% raise every year\n• A new MacBook\n• Your AI tools, on us\n• Health insurance\n• All-day food, on the company\n• Luxury gym membership\n• 24 paid days off\n• Travel and rental allowance\n• Retirement benefit (EOBI)\nHow to apply\nApplying takes 2–5 minutes: a short, casual video on why you fit.\nApply here: https://careers.ccript.com/careers/ae391a4c-3747-4f0f-9ee4-681b2c843333",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488549816": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Job\nRole: Junior Software Engineer\nRole Type: Full-time\nExperience: 1–2 years\nCompensation: $500 USD base salary per month, plus up to $200 USD in performance-based bonuses per month.\nAbout the Role\nSmartPropFirm is looking for a Junior Software Engineer to join our Product & Engineering team.\nYou’ll help build and improve software for the prop trading industry, including trading tools, dashboards, rewards systems, marketplaces, and platform features.\nWe’re looking for someone with strong programming fundamentals who learns quickly, solves problems effectively, and is comfortable using modern development and AI tools.\nResponsibilities\nBuild and improve features across our web platform.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and reliable code.\nWork across frontend and backend based on project needs.\nIntegrate APIs, databases, and third-party services.\nFix bugs, improve performance, and test your work.\nUse AI tools effectively for development, research, and debugging.\nCollaborate with the team and take ownership of assigned tasks.\nRequirements\n1–2 years of software development experience.\nStrong programming fundamentals.\nGood knowledge of JavaScript/TypeScript, React, and Next.js.\nBasic understanding of APIs, databases, and authentication.\nComfortable with Git, code reviews, and existing codebases.\nStrong problem-solving and communication skills.\nExperience with AI development tools such as ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude, or GitHub Copilot.\nNice to Have\nExperience with Next.js, Node.js, WordPress, REST APIs, or SaaS platforms.\nFamiliarity with responsive UI/UX and production debugging.\nExperience or interest in fintech, trading, dashboards, marketplaces, or rewards systems.\nWhy Join SmartPropFirm?\nBuild real products used by traders.\nGain hands-on full-stack development experience.\nLearn from an experienced product and engineering team.\nWork with modern technologies and AI-assisted development.\nGrow quickly in a fast-moving environment where your work has direct impact.\nAdditional Requirements\n1+ years of work experience with software engineering practices.\n1+ years of work experience with Next.js.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488838083": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description\nYuzee connects people with education, careers and employment opportunities. Our platform brings together course discovery, job search, institutions, employers and AI-assisted guidance across web and mobile.\nWe’re looking for a senior, hands-on Angular developer who can take ownership of frontend delivery and help guide our technical direction. You should be comfortable understanding an existing product, identifying what needs improvement and delivering practical, reliable solutions.\nAre you a talented and experienced Angular Developer looking to be part of a dynamic and innovative team? Join us at Yuzee and contribute to the creation of cutting-edge web application that redefine user experiences.\nJob Description\nWhat you’ll do\nDevelop and improve our Angular web applications and contribute to our Ionic/Capacitor mobile app.\nOwn features from understanding requirements through implementation, testing and release verification.\nImprove important user journeys, including search, navigation, conversations, forms and account management.\nDiagnose problems across the interface, application state, APIs and data, and resolve their underlying causes.\nWork closely with backend developers to build clear API contracts, dependable integrations and useful error handling.\nHelp establish consistent architecture, reusable components, coding standards and appropriate automated tests.\nReview code, document important decisions and support other developers.\nRecommend improvements that balance product needs, maintainability, performance and delivery time.\nWhat We’re Looking For\nStrong experience delivering production applications with Angular, TypeScript, RxJS, HTML and CSS.\nA sound understanding of component design, routing, forms, state management and asynchronous behaviour.\nExperience maintaining and improving an established codebase.\nStrong skills in REST API integration, authentication, session handling and debugging.\nExperience with Git, pull requests, code reviews and automated testing.\nAttention to responsive design, accessibility and consistent behaviour across browsers and devices.\nClear communication and the ability to explain technical decisions and trade-offs.\nEvidence of taking responsibility for working software, including investigating issues after release.\nWhat Success Looks Like\nYou understand how the existing platform fits together, help the team agree on sensible priorities and deliver improvements users can depend on. Your changes preserve working journeys, reduce recurring problems and make future development easier.\nQualifications\nGood spoken and written English proficiency\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or Computer Engineering\n4 years experience with front-end development\nAt least 4 years of proven experience with Angular 7 or 8\nProven work experience investigating issues faced by users, identify the root causes and fixing them\n4 years of experience in using Agile work methodologies\nProficient in CSS, HTML, and writing cross-browser compatible codes\n4 years of extensive programming experience in HTML5, CSS3, SASS and Bootstrap\n4 years of experience with REST APIs\nKnowledge of JavaScript MV-VM/MVC frameworks including Angluar JS\nExtensive experience with Node JS and Express JS is a bonus\nGreat project management skills is a bonus\nAbility to work with a multicultural team\nExcellent communication skills\nCritical thinker and good problem-solver\nAdditional Information\nThis is a full-time remote job (You will work from home)\nChallenging work environment and complex project where you can really grow as a professional\nCompany shares can be offered based on how successful with our products' launch\nPromotions towards better job roles possible after a certain period of time",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489496365": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nRevive Business Solutions works with organizations to support business technology and software solutions. The Dealer Management Systems Integration team helps connect applications and services so that information can move reliably between systems. The team contributes to ongoing application development, maintenance, integration, and modernization, with a focus on dependable and maintainable solutions. Team members collaborate across technical and business functions to understand needs, address issues, and deliver improvements.\nAbout The Role\nRevive Business Solutions is seeking an early-career .NET Developer to support its Dealer Management Systems Integration team. This opportunity is suitable for a candidate with approximately one to three years of experience gained through professional employment, an internship, a co-op, academic work, or personal projects. You will contribute to application enhancements, maintenance, testing, API development, and integration support while learning from senior developers, product owners, and team leads.\nThe successful candidate will work through the software development lifecycle in a collaborative Agile environment. You will take on assigned development and troubleshooting tasks, participate in team practices, and build your experience with modern application development and integration. This role calls for curiosity, clear communication, accountability, and a willingness to strengthen technical skills over time.\nQualifications\nA bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Systems, or a related technical field is required. Candidates should have approximately one year or more of exposure to C#, ASP.NET, .NET Core, or object-oriented programming through work, internships, co-op placements, coursework, or projects.\nExperience or familiarity with front-end technologies such as ReactJS, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, or jQuery is valuable. Candidates should understand basic SQL queries and relational database concepts, and have exposure to creating, consuming, testing, or supporting web APIs. Familiarity with REST, JSON payloads, request and response handling, authentication concepts, and API connectivity troubleshooting is desirable; exposure to SOAP services is an asset.\nAdditional useful knowledge includes unit or API testing, debugging, Git, branching, pull requests, and code reviews. Awareness of SOLID principles, clean code, reusable components, application security, performance, scalability, and maintainability is an advantage. Familiarity with Azure DevOps, Azure DevOps Services, Jira, Azure, Kubernetes, or CI/CD concepts is welcome. Academic, open-source, internship, or personal software projects are also relevant.\nResponsibilities\nContribute to enhancements, maintenance, defect resolution, refactoring, and small feature development for existing web applications, following team standards and receiving guidance where appropriate. Assist with building and supporting APIs and integrations between internal and external systems, including data mapping, error handling, logging, and coordination with consuming applications.\nHelp test and validate code, investigate application or connectivity issues, and support data-related troubleshooting. Participate in Agile ceremonies, including sprint planning, daily stand-ups, backlog refinement, and retrospectives. Collaborate with developers, product owners, business partners, and quality assurance colleagues to clarify requirements and share progress. Follow development, deployment, and documentation practices, and contribute to continuous improvement across the software development lifecycle.\nBenefits\nThis role offers the opportunity to develop practical software engineering skills while contributing to real application and systems integration work. You will collaborate with experienced technical and business colleagues, gain exposure to APIs and the .NET ecosystem, and build familiarity with Agile delivery and modernization efforts. The team environment supports continued learning and the gradual development of technical ownership.\nEqual Opportunity\nRevive Business Solutions is committed to providing a respectful and inclusive workplace. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, skills, and business needs. We welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds and encourage candidates who meet the role requirements to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489633576": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the job\nMeeBoss is sharing this role on behalf of Prime Techwings.\nMeeBoss is sharing this active opportunity on behalf of Voltus, a leading company for Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) that aims to be the platform fulfilling the promise of the energy transition.\nThis role is appropriate for entry-level to early-career engineering candidates eager to build scalable software for Voltus.\nYou will join a fully remote team tackling complex energy industry challenges, collaborating with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack, and contributing to core systems that decarbonize the grid.\nJob title\nSoftware Engineer\nLocation\nRemote\nCompensation\nBase pay is $110,000-$140,000 USD annually, commensurate with experience, with a 10% annual bonus and equity.\nWhy this role\nJoin a fully remote team distributed across the US, Canada, and abroad.\nContribute to core systems that decarbonize the grid and provide flexibility, reliability, and resilience to the energy market.\nCollaborate with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack including Python, Postgres, Go, FastAPI, and React.\nWhat you will do\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code to support the team’s projects.\nContribute to the design and implementation of new features and services.\nCollaborate with your team to troubleshoot and resolve issues in the production environment.\nParticipate in code reviews to learn from and contribute to the team’s shared knowledge.\nWork with stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nWhat we are looking for\nA Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent combination of education and experience, in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\nFoundational programming skills in a backend language like Python.\nA strong desire to learn and grow as a software engineer.\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\nA genuine passion for creating a cleaner, more resilient energy future.\nAuthorization to work in the US or Canada without sponsorship.\nA link to your GitHub account in the application (applications without a GitHub account will not be considered).\nBenefits\nUnlimited PTO for full-time employees.\nParental leave.\nComprehensive benefits package to promote health, wellness, and financial security.\nAbout MeeBoss\nMeeBoss helps job seekers and hiring teams make direct, relevant career connections.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490035427": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-13T19:49:53.369185+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nACE Money Transfer is looking for a skilled Laravel Developer to develop, maintain and optimise our web applications using PHP and the Laravel framework .\nYou will build and improve the backend services, RESTful APIs and database layers behind our digital platforms. You will also integrate third-party services and keep our applications secure, scalable and high-performing .\nYou will work closely with frontend developers, QA engineers and the wider technology team, from writing clean code and reviewing pull requests through to deployment and production support.\nThe role reports to [Insert, e.g., Engineering Manager / Tech Lead] . It suits a developer with strong backend skills who takes ownership of their work and wants to grow in a fast-moving fintech environment.\nResponsibilities\nApplication Development\nDevelop, maintain, and improve web applications using PHP and Laravel\nWrite clean, reusable, efficient, and well-structured code\nDesign, build and maintain RESTful APIs and backend services.1\nIntegrate third-party APIs and external services\nDatabase Management\nWork with MySQL databases, including database design and query optimisation\nQuality, Performance & Security\nIdentify, troubleshoot and fix application bugs and performance issues\nKeep applications secure, scalable and performing well\nTake part in code reviews and follow established coding standards\nDeployment & Production Support\nManage application deployments and support production environments\nCollaboration & Documentation\nWork with frontend developers, QA engineers, and other team members\nKeep technical documentation up to date and follow development SOPs\nRequirements\nQualifications & Experience\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field (preferred)\n2–4 years of experience in PHP and Laravel development\nStrong knowledge of PHP and Laravel\nGood understanding of MVC architecture and OOP concepts\nExperience with MySQL and database optimisation\nKnowledge of developing and integrating RESTful APIs\nProficiency in HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Bootstrap\nFamiliarity with Git and version control workflows\nUnderstanding of authentication, authorisation and application security\nExperience with debugging and performance optimisation\nPreferred:\nExperience with Laravel queues, jobs, events and scheduling\nFamiliarity with Redis and caching\nKnowledge of Linux environments and deployment processes\nExperience with third-party integrations and payment gateways\nFamiliarity with Agile/Scrum methods\nSoft Skills & Leadership\nProblem-solving: strong analytical and problem-solving skills\nCommunication and teamwork: works well with developers, QA and stakeholders\nTime management: handles several tasks at once and meets deadlines\nContinuous learning: keen to learn new technologies and build technical skills\nOwnership: works independently and takes responsibility for assigned tasks\nJob Details\nLocation: Lahore/Kharian, Pakistan\nJob Type: Onsite\nWorking Hours / Shift: 01:00 PKT to 10:00 PKT\nDepartment: Technology / Software Development\nAbout ACE Money Transfer\nACE Money Transfer is a UK-based multinational fintech headquartered in Manchester, United Kingdom. We provide fast, secure and affordable online remittance services to customers in 29 countries across the UK, Europe, Canada and Australia, and we enable cross-border money transfers to 100+ countries worldwide.\nEvery day, our platform helps people support their families, pay for education and build better futures across borders. As part of the wider ACE Group, we combine a fast-paced growth culture with strong regulatory standards and a commitment to innovation in digital payments.\nAt ACE you will work with talented, diverse teams across multiple regions and take real ownership of work that matters. You will also help shape the future of global money movement.\nLearn more: ACE Money Transfer Company Profile\nPowered by JazzHR\nQJ9QVNkoph",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
